. Its color and form differ according to its habitat and the quality of its food.'),(10496,422,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Purple mucus sticks to the hands of anyone who touches it. Take care, as the substance is troublesome to wash off.'),(10497,422,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','While they normally live in the sea, they can function on land, too, until their skin dries out.'),(10498,422,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When it senses danger, a purple liquid oozes out of it. The liquid is thought to be something like greasy sweat.'),(10499,422,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon’s habitat shapes its physique. According to some theories, life in warm ocean waters causes this variation to develop.'),(10500,422,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Subjecting this Pokémon to a strong force causes it to secrete a strange purple fluid. Though harmless, the fluid is awfully sticky.'),(10501,422,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Found in abundance on seashores bordering warm waters. Shellos are unexpectedly friendly and will crawl toward any person they see. Take care not to get coated in mucus!'),(10502,423,'diamond','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It has a pliable body without any bones. If any part of its body is torn off, it grows right back.'),(10503,423,'pearl','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It apparently had a huge shell for protection in ancient times. It lives in shallow tidal pools.'),(10504,423,'platinum','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.'),(10505,423,'heartgold','Gen IV (Johto)','When its natural enemy attacks, it oozes purple fluid and escapes.'),(10506,423,'soulsilver','Gen IV (Johto)','When its natural enemy attacks, it oozes purple fluid and escapes.'),(10507,423,'black','Gen V (Unova)','Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.'),(10508,423,'white','Gen V (Unova)','Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are trace