o make people fall in love, so some people search for this Pokémon as if their life depended on it.'),(10731,429,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Feared for its wrath and the curses it spreads, this Pokémon will also, on a whim, cast spells that help people.'),(10732,429,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its muttered curses can cause awful headaches or terrifying visions that torment others.'),(10733,429,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','The incantations Mismagius chants can ward against misfortune, so a custom exists of inviting it into one\'s home. Incur the Pokémon\'s displeasure, however, and disaster will surely ensue.'),(10734,426,'diamond','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It’s drowzy in daytime, but flies off in the evening in big groups. No one knows where they go.'),(10735,426,'pearl','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It carries people and Pokémon when it flies. But since it only drifts, it can end up anywhere.'),(10736,426,'platinum','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','At dusk, swarms of them are carried aloft on winds. When noticed, they suddenly vanish.'),(10737,426,'heartgold','Gen IV (Johto)','It can generate and release gas within its body. That’s how it can control the altitude of its drift.'),(10738,426,'soulsilver','Gen IV (Johto)','It can generate and release gas within its body. That’s how it can control the altitude of its drift.'),(10739,426,'black','Gen V (Unova)','At dusk, swarms of them are carried aloft on winds. When noticed, they suddenly vanish.'),(10740,426,'white','Gen V (Unova)','At dusk, swarms of them are carried aloft on winds. When noticed, they suddenly vanish.'),(10741,426,'black-2','Gen V (Unova)','They carry people and Pokémon, but the wind can catch them, so there can’t be a fixed destination.'),(10742,426,'white-2','Gen V (Unova)','They carry people and Pokémon, but the wind can catch them, so there can’t be a fixed destination.'),(10743,426,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','It carries people and Pokémon when it flies. But since it only drifts, it can end up anywhere.'),(10744,426,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It’s drowsy in daytime, but flies off in the evening in big groups. No one knows where they go.'),(10745,426,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It carries people and Pokémon when it flies. But since it only drifts, it can end up anywhere.'),(10746,426,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It’s drowsy in daytime, but flies off in the evening in big groups. No one knows where they go.'),(10747,426,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','There was once an incident in which a man took a trip riding a Drifblim, only to go missing.'),(10748,426,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Even while under careful observation, large flocks of Drifblim flying at dusk will inexplicably disappear from view.'),(10749,426,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','There’s a rumor that if you catch a Drifblim floating on the wind at dusk, you’ll be carried away to the afterlife.'),(10750,426,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The raw material for the gas inside its body is souls. When its body starts to deflate, it’s thought to carry away people and Pokémon.'),(10751,426,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Some say this Pokémon is a collection of souls burdened with regrets, silently drifting through the dusk.'),(10752,426,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It grabs people and Pokémon and carries them off somewhere. Where do they go? Nobody knows.'),(10753,426,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','It drifts along at dusk, perfectly silent. Its transient, melancholy aspect touches some people deeply—every so often, one will come upon a song or poem devoted to Drifblim.'),(10754,435,'diamond','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It sprays a vile-smelling fluid from the tip of its tail to attack. Its range is over 160 feet.'),(10755,435,'pearl','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It sprays a stinky fluid from its tail. The fluid smells worse the longer it is allowed to fester.'),(10756,435,'platinum','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It attacks by spraying a horribly smelly fluid from the tip of its tail. Attacks from above confound it.'),(10757,435,'heartgold','Gen IV (Johto)','