e. It leaks water that looks like tears when adjusting its moisture level.'),(10799,438,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It does not deal well with water, so it lives in dry locales. Since its surroundings tend to lack greenery, it stands out noticeably.'),(10800,438,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','From its eyes, it can expel excess moisture from its body. This liquid is similar in composition to human sweat.'),(10801,438,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It discharges moisture from its eyes, making it look like it’s crying—apparently an effective way of getting enemies to let down their guard.'),(10802,438,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','If its body gets too damp, it will die. So, in a process reminiscent of sweating, its eyes expel moisture.'),(10803,438,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It expels both sweat and tears from its eyes. The sweat is a little salty, while the tears have a slight bitterness.'),(10804,438,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon lives in dry, rocky areas. As its green spheres dry out, their dull luster increases.'),(10805,438,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Its tears elicit sympathy from those who see them, but do not be deceived! This expulsion of body water is merely a physiological mechanism for keeping itself in good health.'),(10806,441,'diamond','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It can learn and speak human words. If they gather, they all learn the same saying.'),(10807,441,'pearl','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','It keeps rhythm by flicking its tail feathers like a metronome. It imitates human speech.'),(10808,441,'platinum','Gen IV (Sinnoh)','Its tongue is just like a human’s. As a result, it can cleverly mimic human speech.'),(10809,441,'heartgold','Gen IV (Johto)','It mimics the cries of other Pokémon to trick them into thinking it’s one of them. This way they won’t attack it.'),(10810,441,'soulsilver','Gen IV (Johto)','It mimics the cries of other Pokémon to trick them into thinking it’s one of them. This way they won’t attack it.'),(10811,441,'black','Gen V (Unova)','Its