ra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When its tail has gotten dirty from self-cleaning or from cleaning its nest, Minccino spends a whole day washing its tail in clean spring water.'),(12586,572,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle.'),(12587,572,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','They pet each other with their tails as a form of greeting. Of the two, the one whose tail is fluffier is a bit more boastful.'),(12588,574,'black','Gen V (Unova)','Their ribbonlike feelers increase their psychic power. They are always staring at something.'),(12589,574,'white','Gen V (Unova)','They intently observe both Trainers and Pokémon. Apparently, they are looking at something that only Gothita can see.'),(12590,574,'black-2','Gen V (Unova)','It stares intently at everything. It can become so obsessed with watching that it doesn’t notice attacks.'),(12591,574,'white-2','Gen V (Unova)','It stares intently at everything. It can become so obsessed with watching that it doesn’t notice attacks.'),(12592,574,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Their ribbonlike feelers increase their psychic power. They are always staring at something.'),(12593,574,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','They intently observe both Trainers and Pokémon. Apparently, they are looking at something that only Gothita can see.'),(12594,574,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Their ribbonlike feelers increase their psychic power. They are always staring at something.'),(12595,574,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','They intently observe both Trainers and Pokémon. Apparently, they are looking at something that only Gothita can see.'),(12596,574,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Though they’re still only babies, there’s psychic power stored in their ribbonlike feelers, and sometimes they use that power to fight.'),(12597,574,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Even when nobody seems to be around, Gothita can still be heard making a muted cry. Many believ