x','Gen VI (Kalos)','It can distinguish the faintest of scents. It puts its sensitive sense of smell to use by helping pastry chefs in their work.'),(13650,685,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Its sense of smell is 100 million times better than a human’s, so even the faintest scent tells it about everything in the area. It’s like it can see with its nose!'),(13651,685,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It can distinguish the faintest of scents. It puts its sensitive sense of smell to use by helping pastry chefs in their work.'),(13652,685,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Its sense of smell is 100 million times better than a human’s, so even the faintest scent tells it about everything in the area. It’s like it can see with its nose!'),(13653,685,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','By taking in a person’s scent, it can sniff out their mental and physical condition. It’s hoped that this skill will have many medical applications.'),(13654,685,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Slurpuff’s fur contains a lot of air, making it soft to the touch and lighter than it looks.'),(13655,690,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Camouflaged as rotten kelp, they spray liquid poison on prey that approaches unawares and then finish it off.'),(13656,690,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It looks just like rotten kelp. It hides from foes while storing up power for its evolution.'),(13657,690,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Camouflaged as rotten kelp, they spray liquid poison on prey that approaches unawares and then finish it off.'),(13658,690,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It looks just like rotten kelp. It hides from foes while storing up power for its evolution.'),(13659,690,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It vanishes into seaweed and remains perfectly still to avoid attacks from large Pokémon. Rotten seaweed is its main food source.'),(13660,690,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s not good at swimming, so it clings to the seaweed. In the Alola region, it’s often found near Dhelmise.'),(13661,690,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It drifts in the ocean, blending in with floating seaweed. When other Pokémon come to feast on the seaweed, Skrelp feasts on them instead.'),(13662,690,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Skrelp looks like a piece of rotten seaweed, so it can blend in with seaweed drifting on the ocean and avoid being detected by enemies.'),(13663,695,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper.'),(13664,695,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds.'),(13665,695,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper.'),(13666,695,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds.'),(13667,695,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A now-vanished desert culture treasured these Pokémon. Appropriately, when Heliolisk came to the Galar region, treasure came with them.'),(13668,695,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','One Heliolisk basking in the sun with its frill outspread is all it would take to produce enough electricity to power a city.'),(13669,691,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Their poison is strong enough to eat through the hull of a tanker, and they spit it indiscriminately at anything that enters their territory.'),(13670,691,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Tales are told of ships that wander into seas where Dragalge live, never to return.'),(13671,691,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Their poison is strong enough to eat through the hull of a tanker, and they spit it indiscriminately at anything that enters their territory.'),(13672,691,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Tales are told of ships that wander into seas where Dragalge live, never to return.'),(13673,691,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This vicious Pokémon sprays a poisonous liquid on opponents that come near. For whatever reason, it gets along really well with Dhelmise.'),(13674,691,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It blends in with seaweed to ambush its prey and then takes them down with a poisonous liquid strong enough to melt metal.'),(13675,691,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Dragalge uses a poisonous liquid capable of corroding metal to send tankers that enter its territory to the bottom of the sea.'),(13676,691,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Dragalge generates dragon energy by sticking the plume on its head out above the ocean’s surface and bathing it in sunlight.'),(13677,688,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Two Binacle live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock.'),(13678,688,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','They stretch and then contract, yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops. They eat seaweed that washes up on the shoreline.'),(13679,688,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Two Binacle live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock.'),(13680,688,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','They stretch and then contract, yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops. They eat seaweed that washes up on the shoreline.'),(13681,688,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','After two Binacle find a suitably sized rock, they adhere themselves to it and live together. They cooperate to gather food during high tide.'),(13682,688,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If the two don’t work well together, both their offense and defense fall apart. Without good teamwork, they won’t survive.'),(13683,696,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. If something happens that it doesn’t like, it throws a tantrum and runs wild.'),(13684,696,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Its immense jaws have enough destructive force that it can chew up an automobile. It lived 100 million years ago.'),(13685,696,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. If something happens that it doesn’t like, it throws a tantrum and runs wild.'),(13686,696,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Its immense jaws have enough destructive force that it can chew up an automobile. It lived 100 million years ago.'),(13687,696,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its large jaw has incredible destructive power. Some theories suggest that its restored form is different from its form of long ago.'),(13688,696,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Tyrunt is spoiled and selfish. It may just be trying to frolic, but sometimes the ones it’s trying to frolic with are gravely injured.'),(13689,696,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This is an ancient Pokémon, revived in modern times. It has a violent disposition, and it’ll tear apart anything it gets between its hefty jaws.'),(13690,696,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon is selfish and likes to be pampered. It can also inflict grievous wounds on its Trainer just by playing around.'),(13691,692,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.'),(13692,692,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock.'),(13693,692,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.'),(13694,692,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock.'),(13695,692,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its claws occasionally fall off, and it keeps a low profile until they grow back. The meat of its claws is so delicious!'),(13696,692,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It moves around by jetting water from its right pincer. It has a poor sense of balance, so it’s terrible at swimming straight.'),(13697,692,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Clauncher’s claws can fall off during battle, but they’ll regenerate. The meat inside the claws is popular as a delicacy in Galar.'),(13698,692,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','By detonating gas that accumulates in its right claw, this Pokémon launches water like a bullet. This is how Clauncher defeats its enemies.'),(13699,699,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','The diamond-shaped crystals on its body expel air as cold as -240 degrees Fahrenheit, surrounding its enemies and encasing them in ice.'),(13700,699,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Using its diamond-shaped crystals, it can instantly create a wall of ice to block an opponent’s attack.'),(13701,699,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','The diamond-shaped crystals on its body expel air as cold as -240 degrees Fahrenheit, surrounding its enemies and encasing them in ice.'),(13702,699,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Using its diamond-shaped crystals, it can instantly create a wall of ice to block an opponent’s attack.'),(13703,699,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','An Aurorus was found frozen solid within a glacier, just as it appeared long ago, which became quite a big event in the news.'),(13704,699,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This usually quiet and kindly Pokémon has a surface temperature of around –240 degrees Fahrenheit.'),(13705,699,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Aurorus was restored from a fossil. It’s said that when this Pokémon howls, auroras appear in the night sky.'),(13706,699,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When gripped by rage, Aurorus will emanate freezing air, covering everything around it in ice.'),(13707,700,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','It sends a soothing aura from its ribbonlike feelers to calm fights.'),(13708,700,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It wraps its ribbonlike feelers around the arm of its beloved Trainer and walks with him or her.'),(13709,700,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It sends a soothing aura from its ribbonlike feelers to calm fights.'),(13710,700,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It wraps its ribbonlike feelers around the arm of its beloved Trainer and walks with him or her.'),(13711,700,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its ribbonlike feelers give off an aura that weakens hostility in its prey, causing them to let down their guard. Then it attacks.'),(13712,700,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When this Pokémon sights its prey, it swirls its ribbonlike feelers as a distraction. A moment later, it pounces.'),(13713,700,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Once a fight breaks out, it will unflinchingly charge at dragon Pokémon that are many times larger than itself.'),(13714,700,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Sylveon wraps its ribbonlike feelers around its Trainer’s arm because this touch enables it to read its Trainer’s feelings.'),(13715,700,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','By releasing enmity-erasing waves from its ribbonlike feelers, Sylveon stops any conflict.'),(13716,700,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','There’s a Galarian fairy tale that describes a beautiful Sylveon vanquishing a dreadful dragon Pokémon.'),(13717,700,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','It emits a soothing aura from its ribbon-shaped organs. It wraps these appendages around quarrelers to instantly restore calm to the situation.'),(13718,697,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Thanks to its gargantuan jaws, which could shred thick metal plates as if they were paper, it was invincible in the ancient world it once inhabited.'),(13719,697,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Nothing could stop this Pokémon 100 million years ago, so it behaved like a king.'),(13720,697,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Thanks to its gargantuan jaws, which could shred thick metal plates as if they were paper, it was invincible in the ancient world it once inhabited.'),(13721,697,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Nothing could stop this Pokémon 100 million years ago, so it behaved like a king.'),(13722,697,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Complete restoration is impossible, allowing room for theories that its entire body was once covered in a feather-like coat.'),(13723,697,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The king of the ancient world, it can easily crunch a car with the devastating strength of its enormous jaws.'),(13724,697,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon is from about 100,000,000 years ago. It has the presence of a king, vicious but magnificent.'),(13725,697,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','A single bite of Tyrantrum’s massive jaws will demolish a car. This Pokémon was the king of the ancient world.'),(13726,698,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','This ancient Pokémon was restored from part of its body that had been frozen in ice for over 100 million years.'),(13727,698,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','This calm Pokémon lived in a cold land where there were no violent predators like Tyrantrum.'),(13728,698,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','This ancient Pokémon was restored from part of its body that had been frozen in ice for over 100 million years.'),(13729,698,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','This calm Pokémon lived in a cold land where there were no violent predators like Tyrantrum.'),(13730,698,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It lived in cold areas in ancient times. It’s said that when Amaura whinnies, auroras appear in the night sky.'),(13731,698,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Amaura was restored successfully, but it’s not expected to live long because of the heat of the current environment.'),(13732,698,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. In the past, it lived with others of its kind in cold lands where there were fewer predators.'),(13733,698,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Amaura is an ancient Pokémon that has gone extinct. Specimens of this species can sometimes be found frozen in ice.'),(13734,704,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','The weakest Dragon-type Pokémon, it lives in damp, shady places, so its body doesn’t dry out.'),(13735,704,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It’s covered in a slimy membrane that makes any punches or kicks slide off it harmlessly.'),(13736,704,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','The weakest Dragon-type Pokémon, it lives in damp, shady places, so its body doesn’t dry out.'),(13737,704,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It’s covered in a slimy membrane that makes any punches or kicks slide off it harmlessly.'),(13738,704,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The weakest of all Dragon-type Pokémon, it’s unable to breathe if its skin dries out, so it sticks to shady places.'),(13739,704,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its source of protection is its slimy, germ-laden mucous membrane. Anyone who touches it needs some thorough hand-washing.'),(13740,704,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It uses its horns to check out its surroundings. They’re very sensitive, so if you grab them, it will feel a strong shock and be unable to move.'),(13741,704,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its body is mostly water. If it dries out, it will die, so it’s always sitting with perfect stillness in the shade.'),(13742,704,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Because most of its body is water, it will dry up if the weather becomes too arid. It’s considered the weakest dragon Pokémon.'),(13743,704,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Their horns are powerful sensors. As soon as Goomy pick up any sign of enemies, they go into hiding. This is how they’ve survived.'),(13744,704,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Goomy hides away in the shade of trees, where it\'s nice and humid. If the slime coating its body dries out, the Pokémon instantly becomes lethargic.'),(13745,701,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama.'),(13746,701,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.'),(13747,701,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama.'),(13748,701,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.'),(13749,701,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It overwhelms opponents with quick moves, but sometimes it showboats for too long when it’s using a special move and gets itself into a pinch.'),(13750,701,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','In combat, Hawlucha leaps nimbly about, taking advantage of its opponents’ blind spots. It’s also skilled at using superb submission holds.'),(13751,701,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It drives its opponents to exhaustion with its agile maneuvers, then ends the fight with a flashy finishing move.'),(13752,701,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It always strikes a pose before going for its finishing move. Sometimes opponents take advantage of that time to counterattack.');
INSERT INTO `pokemon_lore` VALUES (13753,710,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','The pumpkin body is inhabited by a spirit trapped in this world. As the sun sets, it becomes restless and active.'),(13754,710,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It is said to carry wandering spirits to the place where they belong so they can move on.'),(13755,710,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','The pumpkin body is inhabited by a spirit trapped in this world. As the sun sets, it becomes restless and active.'),(13756,710,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It is said to carry wandering spirits to the place where they belong so they can move on.'),(13757,710,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Spirits that wander this world are placed into Pumpkaboo’s body. They’re then moved on to the afterlife.'),(13758,710,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The light that streams out from the holes in the pumpkin can hypnotize and control the people and Pokémon that see it.'),(13759,708,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','These Pokémon are created when spirits possess rotten tree stumps. They prefer to live in abandoned forests.'),(13760,708,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest.'),(13761,708,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','These Pokémon are created when spirits possess rotten tree stumps. They prefer to live in abandoned forests.'),(13762,708,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest.'),(13763,708,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','These Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died in the forest. Their cries sound like eerie screams.'),(13764,708,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','According to legend, medicine to cure any illness can be made by plucking the green leaves on its head, brewing them, and boiling down the liquid.'),(13765,708,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','By imitating the voice of a child, it causes people to get hopelessly lost deep in the forest. It’s trying to make friends with them.'),(13766,708,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','An unknown spirit came to lodge in a tree stump, creating this Pokémon. A cure-all can be made from an infusion of its green leaves.'),(13767,708,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','After a lost child perished in the forest, their spirit possessed a tree stump, causing the spirit’s rebirth as this Pokémon.'),(13768,708,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','With a voice like a human child’s, it cries out to lure adults deep into the forest, getting them lost among the trees.'),(13769,706,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','This very friendly Dragon-type Pokémon will hug its beloved Trainer, leaving that Trainer covered in sticky slime.'),(13770,706,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It attacks with retractable horns. It throws a punch that’s the equivalent of the force of a hundred pro boxers.'),(13771,706,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','This very friendly Dragon-type Pokémon will hug its beloved Trainer, leaving that Trainer covered in sticky slime.'),(13772,706,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It attacks with retractable horns. It throws a punch that’s the equivalent of the force of a hundred pro boxers.'),(13773,706,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','An amazingly friendly Pokémon, but if left to itself, loneliness overcomes it, and it oozes gooey tears.'),(13774,706,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It gets picked on because it’s meek. But then, whoever teased it gets to feel the full force of its horns and a good swatting from its thick tail.'),(13775,706,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s very friendly toward people. If you grow close to it, Goodra will hug you with its sticky, slime-covered body. Don’t get mad.'),(13776,706,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Underneath its slimy skin is a thick layer of fat, and the combination of the two makes enemies’ attacks slide right off.'),(13777,706,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Sometimes it misunderstands instructions and appears dazed or bewildered. Many Trainers don’t mind, finding this behavior to be adorable.'),(13778,706,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its form of offense is forcefully stretching out its horns. The strikes land 100 times harder than any blow from a heavyweight boxer.'),(13779,706,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Able to freely control the hardness of its metallic shell. It loathes solitude and is extremely clingy—it will fume and run riot if those dearest to it ever leave its side.'),(13780,705,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','It drives away opponents by excreting a sticky liquid that can dissolve anything. Its eyes devolved, so it can’t see anything.'),(13781,705,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Its four horns are a high-performance radar system. It uses them to sense sounds and smells, rather than using ears or a nose.'),(13782,705,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It drives away opponents by excreting a sticky liquid that can dissolve anything. Its eyes devolved, so it can’t see anything.'),(13783,705,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Its four horns are a high-performance radar system. It uses them to sense sounds and smells, rather than using ears or a nose.'),(13784,705,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It has trouble drawing a line between friends and food. It will calmly try to melt and eat even those it gets along well with.'),(13785,705,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon’s mucous can dissolve anything. Toothless, it sprays mucous on its prey. Once they’re nicely dissolved, it slurps them up.'),(13786,705,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It crawls along sluggishly. The swirly protrusion on its back is filled with its brain and other organs.'),(13787,705,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its entire body is covered with gooey mucus that can dissolve anything. Be sure to put gloves on if you’re going to touch it.'),(13788,705,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Although this Pokémon isn’t very strong, its body is coated in a caustic slime that can melt through anything, so predators steer clear of it.'),(13789,705,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The lump on its back contains its tiny brain. It thinks only of food and escaping its enemies.'),(13790,705,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','A creature given to melancholy. I suspect its metallic shell developed as a result of the mucus on its skin reacting with the iron in Hisui\'s water.'),(13791,703,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Born from the temperatures and pressures deep underground, it fires beams from the stone in its head.'),(13792,703,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It has slept underground for hundreds of millions of years since its birth. It’s occasionally found during the excavation of caves.'),(13793,703,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Born from the temperatures and pressures deep underground, it fires beams from the stone in its head.'),(13794,703,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It has slept underground for hundreds of millions of years since its birth. It’s occasionally found during the excavation of caves.'),(13795,703,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Born from the high temperatures and pressures deep underground, it defends itself by firing beams from the jewel part of its body.'),(13796,703,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although this Pokémon is not especially rare, its glittering, jewel-draped body draws attention from people.'),(13797,703,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Some say that deep beneath the surface of the world, a pack of Carbink live with their queen in a kingdom of jewels.'),(13798,703,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','To keep the jewels on their bodies free of tarnish, packs of Carbink use their soft manes to polish one another’s jewels.'),(13799,703,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When beset by attackers, Carbink wipes them all out by firing high-energy beams from the gems embedded in its body.'),(13800,703,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s said that somewhere in the world, there’s a mineral vein housing a large pack of slumbering Carbink. It’s also said that this pack has a queen.'),(13801,709,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave.'),(13802,709,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It’s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.'),(13803,709,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave.'),(13804,709,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It’s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.'),(13805,709,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon is said to devour anyone daring to ravage the forest. To the creatures dwelling in the forest, it offers great kindness.'),(13806,709,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Through its roots, it exerts control over other trees. A deadly curse falls upon anyone cutting down trees in forests where Trevenant dwell.'),(13807,709,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s feared as a ghost of the forest. Lumberjacks bring along Fire types, which Trevenant hates, when they enter the forest.'),(13808,709,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon controls trees via roots stretching from its feet, and it will attack anyone that dares to ravage the forest.'),(13809,709,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','People fear it due to a belief that it devours any who try to cut down trees in its forest, but to the Pokémon it shares its woods with, it’s kind.'),(13810,709,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Small roots that extend from the tips of this Pokémon’s feet can tie into the trees of the forest and give Trevenant control over them.'),(13811,707,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','These key collectors threaten any attackers by fiercely jingling their keys at them.'),(13812,707,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime.'),(13813,707,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','These key collectors threaten any attackers by fiercely jingling their keys at them.'),(13814,707,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime.'),(13815,707,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This even-tempered Pokémon has a habit of collecting keys. It will sneak into people’s homes to steal their keys.'),(13816,707,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It inserts its horn into chinks in metal, absorbing metal ions. For some reason, it collects keys.'),(13817,707,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s unclear why it collects keys, giving it a key makes Klefki very happy. However, it apparently only likes master keys.'),(13818,707,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Long ago it lived in mines, but once the minerals that make up its diet became scarcer, Klefki began appearing in human settlements.'),(13819,707,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon is constantly collecting keys. Entrust a Klefki with important keys, and the Pokémon will protect them no matter what.'),(13820,707,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Klefki sucks in metal ions with the horn topping its head. It seems this Pokémon loves keys so much that its head needed to look like one, too.'),(13821,712,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','It blocks opponents’ attacks with the ice that shields its body. It uses cold air to repair any cracks with new ice.'),(13822,712,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','Using air of -150 degrees Fahrenheit, they freeze opponents solid. They live in herds above the snow line on mountains.'),(13823,712,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It blocks opponents’ attacks with the ice that shields its body. It uses cold air to repair any cracks with new ice.'),(13824,712,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Using air of -150 degrees Fahrenheit, they freeze opponents solid. They live in herds above the snow line on mountains.'),(13825,712,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','They chill the air around them to −150 degrees Fahrenheit, freezing the water in the air into ice that they use as armor.'),(13826,712,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon lives in areas of 