waves to detect which fruits are ripe.'),(13879,714,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','After nightfall, they emerge from the caves they nest in during the day. Using their ultrasonic waves, they go on the hunt for ripened fruit.'),(13880,714,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','No wavelength of sound is beyond Noibat’s ability to produce. The ultrasonic waves it generates can overcome much larger Pokémon.'),(13881,720,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','This troublemaker sends anything and everything to faraway places using its loop, which can warp space.'),(13882,720,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It gathers things it likes and passes them through its loop to teleport them to a secret place.'),(13883,720,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','In its true form, it possess a huge amount of power. Legends of its avarice tell how it once carried off an entire castle to gain the treasure hidden within.'),(13884,720,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It is said to be able to seize anything it desires with its six rings and six huge arms. With its power sealed, it is transformed into a much smaller form.'),(13885,702,'x','Gen VI (Kalos)','Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.'),(13886,702,'y','Gen VI (Kalos)','It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers.'),(13887,702,'omega-ruby','Gen VI (Hoenn)','Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.'),(13888,702,'alpha-sapphire','Gen VI (Hoenn)','It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers.'),(13889,702,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It sneaks into people’s homes and steals electricity from their outlets. When your electric bill seems off, it’s the handiwork of this rascal.'),(13890,702,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its upper whiskers are sensors that survey its surroundings. Its lower whiskers are organs that shoot electricity.'),(13891,702,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A Dedenne’s whiskers pick up electrical waves other Dedenne send out. These Pokémon share locations of food or electricity with one another.'),(13892,702,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Since Dedenne can’t generate much electricity on its own, it steals electricity from outlets or other electric Pokémon.'),(13893,724,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It fires arrow quills from its wings with such precision, they can pierce a pebble at distances over a hundred yards.'),(13894,724,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although basically cool and cautious, when it’s caught by surprise, it’s seized by panic.'),(13895,724,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It nocks its arrow quills and shoots them at opponents. When it simply can’t afford to miss, it tugs the vine on its head to improve its focus.'),(13896,724,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Decidueye can nock and fire an arrow at an enemy in a tenth of a second, so its battles are decided in the blink of an eye.'),(13897,724,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','As if wielding a bow, it launches the arrow quills hidden among the feathers of its wings. Decidueye’s shots never miss.'),(13898,724,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','In a tenth of a second, it can nock and fire an arrow quill, piercing an opponent’s weak point before they notice what’s happening.'),(13899,724,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','The air stored inside the rachises of Decidueye\'s feathers insulates the Pokémon against Hisui\'s extreme cold. This is firm proof that evolution can be influenced by environment.'),(13900,725,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','While grooming itself, it builds up fur inside its stomach. It sets the fur alight and spews fiery attacks, which change based on how it coughs.'),(13901,725,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It doesn’t allow its emotions to be easily seen. Earning its trust takes time. It prefers solitude.'),(13902,725,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','If you try too hard to get close to it, it won’t open up to you. Even if you do grow close, giving it too much affection is still a no-no.'),(13903,725,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its coat regrows twice a year. When the time comes, Litten sets its own body on fire and burns away the old fur.'),(13904,725,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It spends even the smallest amount of downtime grooming its fur with its tongue. Loose fur gathers in its stomach and serves as fuel for fiery moves.'),(13905,725,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Trying to pet Litten before it trusts you will result in a nasty scratch from its sharp claws. Be careful.'),(13906,722,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This wary Pokémon uses photosynthesis to store up energy during the day, while becoming active at night.'),(13907,722,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Silently it glides, drawing near its targets. Before they even notice it, it begins to pelt them with vicious kicks.'),(13908,722,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It sends its feathers, which are as sharp as blades, flying in attack. Its legs are strong, so its kicks are also formidable.'),(13909,722,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It feels relaxed in tight, dark places and has been known to use its Trainer’s pocket or bag as a nest.'),(13910,722,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','At a distance, it launches its sharp feathers while flying about. If the enemy gets too close, Rowlet switches tactics and delivers vicious kicks.'),(13911,722,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','During the day, it builds up energy via photosynthesis. At night, it flies silently through the sky, on the prowl for prey.'),(13912,722,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Flies noiselessly on delicate wings. It has mastered the art of deftly launching dagger-sharp feathers from those same wings.'),(13913,723,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A bit of a dandy, it spends its free time preening its wings. Its preoccupation with any dirt on its plumage can leave it unable to battle.'),(13914,723,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It throws sharp feathers called blade quills at enemies or prey. It seldom misses.'),(13915,723,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This narcissistic Pokémon is a clean freak. If you don’t groom it diligently, it will stop listening to you.'),(13916,723,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Supremely sensitive to the presence of others, it can detect opponents standing behind it, flinging its sharp feathers to take them out.'),(13917,723,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It throws one knifelike feather after another at its enemies, and each one precisely strikes a weak point. These feathers are known as blade quills.'),(13918,723,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It never slacks when it comes to the task of cleaning its feathers. Thorough preening keeps it looking spiffy and its blade quills nice and sharp.'),(13919,723,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Regularly basks in sunlight to gather power—presumably due to the frigid climate. Nonetheless, the edges of the blade quills set into its wings are keen as ever.'),(13920,726,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','At its throat, it bears a bell of fire. The bell rings brightly whenever this Pokémon spits fire.'),(13921,726,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It boasts powerful front legs. With a single punch, it can bend an iron bar right over.'),(13922,726,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It can act spoiled if it grows close to its Trainer. A powerful Pokémon, its sharp claws can leave its Trainer’s whole body covered in scratches.'),(13923,726,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When its mane is standing on end, you can tell it’s feeling good. When it isn’t feeling well, its fur will lie down flat.'),(13924,726,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','In the midst of battle, the fire pouch on Torracat’s neck rings like a bell and produces stronger flames than usual.'),(13925,726,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When facing a powerful enemy, Torracat’s fighting spirit gets pumped up, and its fire bell blazes hotter.'),(13926,731,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It can peck at a rate of 16 times a second to drill holes in trees. It uses the holes for food storage and for nesting.'),(13927,731,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon feeds on berries, whose leftover seeds become the ammunition for the attacks it fires off from its mouth.'),(13928,731,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It pecks at trees with its hard beak. You can get some idea of its mood or condition from the rhythm of its pecking.'),(13929,731,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It may look spindly, but its neck muscles are heavy-duty. It can peck at a tree 16 times per second!'),(13930,729,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A skillful dancer, it creates a sequence of water balloons as it dances, and briskly bombards its enemies.'),(13931,729,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It cares deeply for its companions. When its Trainer is feeling down, it performs a cheery dance to try and help.'),(13932,729,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It gets excited when it sees a dance it doesn’t know. This hard worker practices diligently until it can learn that dance.'),(13933,729,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It attacks by smacking its enemies with the exploding water balloons that it creates.'),(13934,729,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','As if dancing, it artfully dodges the attacks of its enemies. All the while, it’s busy forming a bunch of balloons to overwhelm its foes.'),(13935,729,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','On nights when the sea is calm, Brionne dance with one another to the singing of the Primarina that’s leading them.'),(13936,727,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon has a violent, selfish disposition. If it’s not in the mood to listen, it will ignore its Trainer’s orders with complete nonchalance.'),(13937,727,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','After hurling ferocious punches and flinging furious kicks, it finishes opponents off by spewing fire from around its navel.'),(13938,727,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s rough mannered and egotistical, it finds beating down unworthy opponents boring. It gets motivated for stronger opponents.'),(13939,727,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When its fighting spirit is set alight, the flames around its waist become especially intense.'),(13940,727,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It excels at violent, no-holds-barred battles. The temperature of the flames that issue from its navel exceeds 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit.'),(13941,727,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Incineroar’s rough and aggressive behavior is its most notable trait, but the way it helps out small Pokémon shows that it has a kind side as well.'),(13942,728,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon snorts body fluids from its nose, blowing balloons to smash into its foes. It’s famous for being a hard worker.'),(13943,728,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon can control water bubbles. It practices diligently so it can learn to make big bubbles.'),(13944,728,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The balloons it inflates with its nose grow larger and larger as it practices day by day.'),(13945,728,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Popplio gets on top of its bouncy water balloons to jump higher. It’s quite the acrobatic fighter!'),(13946,728,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It creates special bouncy balloons to send at its opponents. When the balloons pop, the sheer force of their bursting is what deals damage.'),(13947,728,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If Popplio want to create big, powerful balloons, they must be persistent. It takes daily practice for these Pokémon to develop their skills.'),(13948,735,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it finds a trace of its prey, it patiently stakes out the location...but it’s always snoozing by nightfall.'),(13949,735,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It adores having Rattata and Raticate for dinner, but as it’s diurnal, it never encounters them. This Pokémon boasts incredible patience.'),(13950,735,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it wasn’t originally found in Alola, this Pokémon was brought over a long time ago when there was a huge Rattata outbreak.'),(13951,735,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Patient by nature, this Pokémon loses control of itself and pounces when it spots its favorite meal—Rattata!'),(13952,732,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It eats berries and stores their seeds in its beak. When it encounters enemies or prey, it fires off all the seeds in a burst.'),(13953,732,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','By bending its beak, it can produce a variety of calls and brand itself a noisy nuisance for its neighbors.'),(13954,732,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It can bend the tip of its beak to produce over a hundred different cries at will.'),(13955,732,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','From its mouth, it fires the seeds of berries it has eaten. The scattered seeds give rise to new plants.'),(13956,734,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','With its sharp fangs, it will bite anything. It did not originally live in Alola but was imported from another region.'),(13957,734,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It wanders around in a never-ending search for food. At dusk, it collapses from exhaustion and falls asleep on the spot.'),(13958,734,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its stomach takes up most of its long torso. It’s a big eater, so the amount Trainers have to spend on its food is no laughing matter.'),(13959,734,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it will eat anything, it prefers fresh living things, so it marches down streets in search of prey.'),(13960,730,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It controls its water balloons with song. The melody is learned from others of its kind and is passed down from one generation to the next.'),(13961,730,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its singing voice is its chief weapon in battle. This Pokémon’s Trainer must prioritize the daily maintenance of its throat at all costs.'),(13962,730,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','To Primarina, every battle is a stage. It takes down its prey with beautiful singing and dancing.'),(13963,730,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Also known as a songstress, it has a fantastical look on moonlit nights when it leads its colony in song.'),(13964,730,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','With its mouth, it makes sonic waves that sound like beautiful singing. It uses the sonic waves to control its water balloons.'),(13965,730,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','For Primarina, every battle’s a stage. Its singing and the dancing of its balloons will mesmerize the audience.'),(13966,738,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It zips around, on sharp lookout for an opening. It concentrates electrical energy within its large jaws and uses it to zap its enemies.'),(13967,738,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It produces electricity via an electrical organ in its abdomen. It overwhelms bird Pokémon with shocking beams of electrical energy.'),(13968,738,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It has an organ that generates electricity in its abdomen. It concentrates energy in its strong jaws and fires off powerful jolts of electricity.'),(13969,738,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Vikavolt flusters opponents with acrobatic flying maneuvers. This creates an opening for it to deliver an electric beam attack.'),(13970,738,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It builds up electricity in its abdomen, focuses it through its jaws, and then fires the electricity off in concentrated beams.'),(13971,738,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If it carries a Charjabug to use as a spare battery, a flying Vikavolt can rapidly fire high-powered beams of electricity.'),(13972,739,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','While guarding its weak points with its pincers, it looks for an opening and unleashes punches. When it loses, it foams at the mouth and faints.'),(13973,739,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It punches so much, its pincers often come off from overuse, but they grow back quickly. What little meat they contain is rich and delicious.'),(13974,739,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its hard pincers are well suited to both offense and defense. Fights between two Crabrawler are like boxing matches.'),(13975,739,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Crabrawler has been known to mistake Exeggutor for a coconut tree and climb it. The enraged Exeggutor shakes it off and stomps it.'),(13976,742,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It feeds on the nectar and pollen of flowers. Because it’s able to sense auras, it can identify which flowers are about to bloom.'),(13977,742,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Myriads of Cutiefly flutter above the heads of people who have auras resembling those of flowers.'),(13978,742,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Nectar and pollen are its favorite fare. In fields of flowers, it gets into skirmishes with Butterfree over food.'),(13979,742,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Cutiefly can pick up the auras of living things. It skillfully reads those auras to predict its foes’ movements and make fools of them.'),(13980,742,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Nectar and pollen are its favorite fare. You can find Cutiefly hovering around Gossifleur, trying to get some of Gossifleur’s pollen.'),(13981,742,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','An opponent’s aura can tell Cutiefly what that opponent’s next move will be. Then Cutiefly can glide around the attack and strike back.'),(13982,743,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It rolls up pollen into puffs. It makes many different varieties, some used as food and others used in battle.'),(13983,743,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Some of Ribombee’s pollen puffs are highly nutritious. They are sometimes sold as supplements.'),(13984,743,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Rain makes pollen damp, so Ribombee hates rain. When it sees ominous clouds, it finds a hollow in a tree, where it waits stock-still.'),(13985,743,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It can predict the weather from moisture levels and wind direction. Ribombee only reveals itself when there are a few clear days in a row.'),(13986,743,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It makes pollen puffs from pollen and nectar. The puffs’ effects depend on the type of ingredients and how much of each one is used.'),(13987,743,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Ribombee absolutely hate getting wet or rained on. In the cloudy Galar region, they are very seldom seen.'),(13988,745,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its quick movements confuse its enemies. Well equipped with claws and fangs, it also uses the sharp rocks in its mane as weapons.'),(13989,745,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When properly raised from a young age, it will become a trustworthy partner that will absolutely never betray its Trainer.'),(13990,745,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The sharp rocks in its mane can cut like knives. Lycanroc wears its prey down by degrees before finishing them off.'),(13991,745,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The rocks in its mane are sharper than a knife. Fragments that break off are treasured as good luck charms.'),(13992,745,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Lycanroc is calm and cautious. The rocks jutting from its mane are razor sharp.'),(13993,745,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','With swift movements, this Pokémon gradually backs its prey into a corner. Lycanroc’s fangs are always aimed toward opponents’ weak spots.'),(13994,740,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It aimed for the top but got lost and ended up on a snowy mountain. Being forced to endure the cold, this Pokémon evolved and grew fur.'),(13995,740,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It just throws punches indiscriminately. In times of desperation, it can lop off its own pincers and fire them like rockets.'),(13996,740,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It stores coldness in its pincers and pummels its foes. It can even smash thick walls of ice to bits!'),(13997,740,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Before it stops to think, it just starts pummeling. There are records of its turning back avalanches with a flurry of punches.'),(13998,741,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It beats its wings together to create fire. As it moves in the steps of its beautiful dance, it bathes opponents in intense flames.'),(13999,741,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Oricorio has sipped red nectar. Its passionate dance moves cause its enemies to combust in both body and mind.'),(14000,741,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It wins the hearts of its enemies with its passionate dancing and then uses the opening it creates to burn them up with blazing flames.'),(14001,741,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Oricorio has drunk red nectar. If its Trainer gives the wrong order, this passionate Pokémon becomes fiercely angry.'),(14002,746,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it’s in trouble, its eyes moisten and begin to shine. The shining light attracts its comrades, and they stand together against their enemies.'),(14003,746,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s awfully weak and notably tasty, so everyone is always out to get it. As it happens, anyone trying to bully it receives a painful lesson.'),(14004,746,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','They’re weak, so they move in schools. However, they can also often be seen all alone, having strayed from the school.'),(14005,746,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When it’s in a jam, its shining eyes attract others of its kind. The light from its eyes is visible almost 25 miles away.'),(14006,746,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Individually, they’re incredibly weak. It’s by gathering up into schools that they’re able to confront opponents.'),(14007,746,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it senses danger, its eyes tear up. The sparkle of its tears signals other Wishiwashi to gather.'),(14008,744,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s considered to be a good Pokémon for beginners because of its friendliness, but its disposition grows rougher as it grows up.'),(14009,744,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon has lived with people since times long ago. It can sense when its Trainer is in the dumps and will stick close by its Trainer’s side.'),(14010,744,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','As they develop, their disposition grows more violent and aggressive. Many Trainers find them too much to handle and abandon them.'),(14011,744,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When it rubs the rocks on its neck against you, that’s proof of its love for you. However, the rocks are sharp, so the gesture is quite painful!'),(14012,744,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon can bond very strongly with its Trainer, but it also has a habit of biting. Raising a Rockruff for a long time can be challenging.'),(14013,744,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon intimidates opponents by striking the ground with the rocks on its neck. The moment an opponent flinches, Rockruff attacks.'),(14014,733,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it battles, its beak heats up. The temperature can easily exceed 212 degrees Fahrenheit, causing severe burns when it hits.'),(14015,733,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Within its beak, its internal gas ignites, explosively launching seeds with enough power to pulverize boulders.'),(14016,733,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','They smack beaks with others of their kind to communicate. The strength and number of hits tell each other how they feel.'),(14017,733,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Known for forming harmonious couples, this Pokémon is brought to wedding ceremonies as a good luck charm.'),(14018,747,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It plunges the poison spike on its head into its prey. When the prey has weakened, Mareanie deals the finishing blow with its 10 tentacles.'),(14019,747,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s found crawling on beaches and seafloors. The coral that grows on Corsola’s head is as good as a five-star banquet to this Pokémon.'),(14020,747,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','They eat Corsola branches, so Mareanie are hated by craftsmen who work with Corsola branches that have naturally fallen off.'),(14021,747,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Aside from its head, its body parts regenerate quickly if they’re cut off. After a good night’s sleep, Mareanie is back to normal.'),(14022,747,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The first symptom of its sting is numbness. The next is an itching sensation so intense that it’s impossible to resist the urge to claw at your skin.'),(14023,747,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Unlike their Alolan counterparts, the Mareanie of the Galar region have not yet figured out that the branches of Corsola are delicious.'),(14024,748,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Toxapex crawls along the ocean floor on its 12 legs. It leaves a trail of Corsola bits scattered in its wake.'),(14025,748,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Those attacked by Toxapex’s poison will suffer intense pain for three days and three nights. Post-recovery, there will be some aftereffects.'),(14026,748,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','To attack, this Pokémon sends toxic spikes flying at its enemies. Ones that come close get mown down by the claws on its feet.'),(14027,748,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','With its 12 legs, it creates a dome to shelter within. The flow of the tides doesn’t affect Toxapex in there, so it’s very comfortable.'),(14028,748,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','To survive in the cold waters of Galar, this Pokémon forms a dome with its legs, enclosing its body so it can capture its own body heat.'),(14029,748,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Within the poison sac in its body is a poison so toxic that Pokémon as large as Wailord will still be suffering three days after it first takes effect.'),(14030,749,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The mud stuck to Mudbray’s hooves enhances its grip and its powerful running gait.'),(14031,749,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It has a stubborn, individualistic disposition. Eating dirt, making mud, and playing in the mire all form part of its daily routine.'),(14032,749,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It loves playing in the mud. If it isn’t showered with mud on a daily basis, it gets stressed out and stops listening to its Trainer.'),(14033,749,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Possessing mighty power, Mudbray can be loaded with 50 times its own body weight and will be totally fine.'),(14034,749,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Loads weighing up to 50 times as much as its own body weight pose no issue for this Pokémon. It’s skilled at making use of mud.'),(14035,749,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It eats dirt to create mud and smears this mud all over its feet, giving them the grip needed to walk on rough terrain without slipping.'),(14036,750,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It spits a mud that provides resistance to both wind and rain, so the walls of old houses were often coated with it.'),(14037,750,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its heavy, mud-covered kicks are its best means of attack, and it can reduce large trucks to scrap without breaking a sweat.'),(14038,750,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It remains calm and unmoving no matter the situation. It mixes dirt with the saliva in its mouth to make a special kind of mud.'),(14039,750,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It can trudge mountain roads without rest for three days and three nights, all the while dragging a 10-ton load.'),(14040,750,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Mud that hardens around a Mudsdale’s legs sets harder than stone. It’s so hard that it allows this Pokémon to scrap a truck with a single kick.'),(14041,750,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Mudsdale has so much stamina that it could carry over 10 tons across the Galar region without rest or sleep.'),(14042,736,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its strong jaw enables it to scrape trees and slurp out the sap. It normally lives underground.'),(14043,736,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','They often gather near places frequented by electric Pokémon in order to avoid being attacked by bird Pokémon.'),(14044,736,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','If you find its nest, you shouldn’t stick your hand inside. You’ll get bitten by an irritated Grubbin.'),(14045,736,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It spits a sticky thread to stop opponents in their tracks, and then it grabs them in its sharp, sturdy mandibles to take them down.'),(14046,736,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its natural enemies, like Rookidee, may flee rather than risk getting caught in its large mandibles that can snap thick tree branches.'),(14047,736,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It uses its big jaws to dig nests into the forest floor, and it loves to feed on sweet tree sap.'),(14048,737,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its body is capable of storing electricity. On camping trips, people are grateful to have one around.'),(14049,737,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','From the food it digests, it generates electricity, and it stores this energy in its electric sac.'),(14050,737,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It buries itself in fallen leaves and barely moves, munching away on humus. If you accidentally step on one, you’ll get a shock!'),(14051,737,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its stout shell provides excellent defense from attacks. It uses electricity on persistent opponents.'),(14052,737,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','While its durable shell protects it from attacks, Charjabug strikes at enemies with jolts of electricity discharged from the tips of its jaws.'),(14053,737,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its digestive processes convert the leaves it eats into electricity. An electric sac in its belly stores the electricity for later use.'),(14054,758,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','For some reason, only females have been found. It creates a reverse harem of male Salandit that it lives with.'),(14055,758,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Filled with pheromones, its poisonous gas can be diluted to use in the production of luscious perfumes.'),(14056,758,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Salazzle lives deep in caves and forces the Salandit it has attracted with its pheromones to serve it.'),(14057,758,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It punishes Salandit that couldn’t bring it food with a fierce slap of its flame-spewing palm.'),(14058,758,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Only female Salazzle exist. They emit a gas laden with pheromones to captivate male Salandit.'),(14059,758,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The winner of competitions between Salazzle is decided by which one has the most male Salandit with it.'),(14060,760,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This immensely dangerous Pokémon possesses overwhelming physical strength. Its habitat is generally off-limits.'),(14061,760,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon has the habit of hugging its companions. Many Trainers have left this world after their spines were squashed by its hug.'),(14062,760,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It waves its hands wildly in intimidation and warning. Life is over for anyone who doesn’t run away as fast as possible.'),(14063,760,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It boasts tremendous physical strength. Many people call it the most dangerous Pokémon in the Alola region.'),(14064,760,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Once it accepts you as a friend, it tries to show its affection with a hug. Letting it do that is dangerous—it could easily shatter your bones.'),(14065,760,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The moves it uses to take down its prey would make a martial artist jealous. It tucks subdued prey under its arms to carry them to its nest.'),(14066,755,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It scatters spores that flicker and glow. Anyone seeing these lights falls into a deep slumber.'),(14067,755,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','As it drowses the day away, it nourishes itself by sucking from tree roots. It wakens at the fall of night, wandering off in search of a new tree.'),(14068,755,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It scatters its shining spores around itself. Even though they’re dangerous, nighttime tours of forests where Morelull live are popular.'),(14069,755,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It likes damp dark places. When night falls, the spores filling the caps of its mushrooms glow.'),(14070,755,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Pokémon living in the forest eat the delicious caps on Morelull’s head. The caps regrow overnight.'),(14071,755,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Morelull live in forests that stay dark even during the day. They scatter flickering spores that put enemies to sleep.'),(14072,757,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It burns its bodily fluids to create a poisonous gas. When its enemies become disoriented from inhaling the gas, it attacks them.'),(14073,757,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Volcanoes or dry, craggy places are its home. It emanates a sweet-smelling poisonous gas that attracts bug Pokémon, then attacks them.'),(14074,757,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The males will do whatever the females tell them. They give the females most of their food. Due to malnutrition, the males can’t evolve.'),(14075,757,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It weakens opponents and sends them reeling with its poisonous gas. Salandit doesn’t deal well with Spinda, since it’s always reeling.'),(14076,757,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its venom sacs produce a fluid that this Pokémon then heats up with the flame in its tail. This process creates Salandit’s poisonous gas.'),(14077,757,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This sneaky Pokémon will slink behind its prey and immobilize it with poisonous gas before the prey even realizes Salandit is there.'),(14078,759,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Despite its adorable appearance, when it gets angry and flails about, its arms and legs could knock a pro wrestler sprawling.'),(14079,759,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A touch from anyone except a known friend sends it into a surging frenzy. It’s an incredibly dangerous Pokémon.'),(14080,759,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It boasts power enough to split large trees in half. The organ on its rear releases an odor that it uses to communicate with others of its kind.'),(14081,759,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Stufful hates to be hugged or touched in any way. It will squirm, thrash, and resist with amazing power.'),(14082,759,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its fluffy fur is a delight to pet, but carelessly reaching out to touch this Pokémon could result in painful retaliation.'),(14083,759,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The way it protects itself by flailing its arms may be an adorable sight, but stay well away. This is flailing that can snap thick tree trunks.'),(14084,753,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','During the day, it sleeps and soaks up light. When night falls, it walks around looking for a safer place to sleep.'),(14085,753,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','They give off a sweet and refreshing scent. Cutiefly often gather near the tall grass where Fomantis are hiding.'),(14086,753,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When the sun rises, Fomantis spreads its four leaves and bathes in the sunlight. The tip of its head has a pleasant aroma.'),(14087,753,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It loves the sunshine. When it basks in the sunlight regularly, it grows up with vivid coloration.'),(14088,753,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When bathed in sunlight, this Pokémon emits a pleasantly sweet scent, which causes bug Pokémon to gather around it.'),(14089,753,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','During the day, Fomantis basks in sunlight and sleeps peacefully. It wakes and moves around at night.'),(14090,751,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It crawls onto the land in search of food. Its water bubble allows it to breathe and protects its soft head.'),(14091,751,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When it comes across enemies or potential prey, this Pokémon smashes its water-bubble-covered head into them.'),(14092,751,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When two Dewpider meet, they display their water bubbles to each other. Then the one with the smaller bubble gets out of the other’s way.'),(14093,751,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It can only breathe oxygen that has dissolved in water, so it wears a water bubble on its head when it walks around on land.'),(14094,751,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It forms a water bubble at the rear of its body and then covers its head with it. Meeting another Dewpider means comparing water-bubble sizes.'),(14095,751,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Dewpider normally lives underwater. When it comes onto land in search of food, it takes water with it in the form of a bubble on its head.'),(14096,752,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It delivers headbutts with the water bubble on its head. Small Pokémon get sucked into the bubble, where they drown.'),(14097,752,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Despite what its appearance suggests, it cares for others. If it finds vulnerable, weak Pokémon, it protectively brings them into its water bubble.'),(14098,752,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It usually passes its time in the water. When its belly is full, it stores its subdued prey in the water bubble on its head.'),(14099,752,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It has a habit of storing things it values in its water bubble. If its Trainer doesn’t watch out, Araquanid will try to put them in its bubble!'),(14100,752,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It launches water bubbles with its legs, drowning prey within the bubbles. This Pokémon can then take its time to savor its meal.'),(14101,752,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It acts as a caretaker for Dewpider, putting them inside its bubble and letting them eat any leftover food.'),(14102,754,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It requires a lot of effort to maintain Lurantis’s vivid coloring, but some collectors enjoy this work and treat it as their hobby.'),(14103,754,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It fires beams from its sickle-shaped petals. These beams are powerful enough to cleave through thick metal plates.'),(14104,754,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','For self-protection, it pretends to be a bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear keen-edged petals.'),(14105,754,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','As it slashes into its enemies, it looks like it’s dancing. Its elegant appearance has led some to call it the most glamorous Grass Pokémon.'),(14106,754,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon resembles a beautiful flower. A properly raised Lurantis will have gorgeous, brilliant colors.'),(14107,754,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The petals on this Pokémon’s arms are thin and super sharp, and they can fire laser beams if Lurantis gathers light first.'),(14108,764,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It attaches flowers to its highly nutritious vine. This revitalizes the flowers, and they give off an aromatic scent.'),(14109,764,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Baths prepared with the flowers from its vine have a relaxing effect, so this Pokémon is a hit with many people.'),(14110,764,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It stretches sticky vines out from its head and picks flowers to adorn itself with. When it doesn’t have any flowers, it feels uneasy.'),(14111,764,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It picks flowers and sticks them to its body with fluids it produces. The aroma that wafts from its petals has a healing effect.'),(14112,764,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Comfey picks flowers with its vine and decorates itself with them. For some reason, flowers won’t wither once they’re attached to a Comfey.'),(14113,764,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','These Pokémon smell very nice. All Comfey wear different flowers, so each of these Pokémon has its own individual scent.'),(14114,761,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A delectable aroma pours from its body. They are often swallowed whole by Toucannon lured by that wafting deliciousness.'),(14115,761,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s too sugary for human consumption, Bounsweet’s sweat can be watered down into a juice with just the right amount of sweetness.'),(14116,761,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Because of its sweet, delicious aroma, bird Pokémon are always after it, but it’s not intelligent enough to care.'),(14117,761,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It tries to resist being swallowed by a bird Pokémon by spinning the sepals on its head. It’s usually a fruitless attempt.'),(14118,761,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its body gives off a sweet, fruity scent that is extremely appetizing to bird Pokémon.'),(14119,761,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When under attack, it secretes a sweet and delicious sweat. The scent only calls more enemies to it.'),(14120,768,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','With a flashing slash of its giant sharp claws, it cleaves seawater—or even air—right in two.'),(14121,768,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It battles skillfully with its six arms, but spends most of its time peacefully meditating in caves deep beneath the sea.'),(14122,768,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The shell covering its body is as hard as diamond. This Pokémon will do anything it takes to win.'),(14123,768,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its claws, which it can extend and retract at will, are its greatest weapons. Golisopod is sometimes accompanied by Wimpod.'),(14124,768,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It will do anything to win, taking advantage of every opening and finishing opponents off with the small claws on its front legs.'),(14125,768,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','They live in sunken ships or in holes in the seabed. When Golisopod and Grapploct battle, the loser becomes the winner’s meal.'),(14126,770,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Possessed people controlled by this Pokémon transformed its sand mound into a castle. As it evolved, its power to curse grew ever stronger.'),(14127,770,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Buried beneath the castle are masses of dried-up bones from those whose vitality it has drained.'),(14128,770,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Each of its grains of sand has its own will. Palossand eats small Pokémon and siphons away their vital essence while they’re still alive.'),(14129,770,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Once it has whipped up a sandstorm to halt its opponents in their tracks, this terrifying Pokémon snatches away their vitality.'),(14130,770,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Palossand is known as the Beach Nightmare. It pulls its prey down into the sand by controlling the sand itself, and then it sucks out their souls.'),(14131,770,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon lives on beaches, but it hates water. Palossand can’t maintain its castle-like shape if it gets drenched by a heavy rain.'),(14132,769,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Born from a sand mound playfully built by a child, this Pokémon embodies the grudges of the departed.'),(14133,769,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It takes control of anyone who puts a hand in its mouth. And so it adds to the accumulation of its sand-mound body.'),(14134,769,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It likes the shovel on its head, so Sandygast will get serious and fight any children who come to take it back.'),(14135,769,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','If you build sand mounds when you’re playing, destroy them before you go home, or they may get possessed and become Sandygast.'),(14136,769,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Grudges of the dead have possessed a mound of sand and become a Pokémon. Sandygast is fond of the shovel on its head.'),(14137,769,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Sandygast mainly inhabits beaches. It takes control of anyone who puts their hand into its mouth, forcing them to make its body bigger.'),(14138,762,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The sepals on its head developed to protect its body. These are quite hard, so even if pecked by bird Pokémon, this Pokémon is totally fine.'),(14139,762,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon is always bouncing around energetically. Other Pokémon are attracted by its lively appearance and pleasant aroma.'),(14140,762,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It’s protected by its hard sepals, so it plays with bird Pokémon without worry. They peck it relentlessly, but it doesn’t care.'),(14141,762,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It bounces around, swinging the sepals on its head with abandon. They’re quite painful when they smack you!'),(14142,762,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','As it twirls like a dancer, a sweet smell spreads out around it. Anyone who inhales the scent will feel a surge of happiness.'),(14143,762,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Any Corvisquire that pecks at this Pokémon will be greeted with a smack from its sepals followed by a sharp kick.'),(14144,767,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon is a coward. As it desperately dashes off, the flailing of its many legs leaves a sparkling clean path in its wake.'),(14145,767,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its habitat varies from beaches to seabeds. A natural scavenger, it will gleefully chow down on anything edible, no matter how rotten.'),(14146,767,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It will pick up anything it finds on the ground. Sometimes it finds coins, so Murkrow and Meowth will go after it.'),(14147,767,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','An astonishingly cowardly Pokémon, Wimpod will whir its legs at high speeds to run away if anything comes near it.'),(14148,767,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s nature’s cleaner—it eats anything and everything, including garbage and rotten things. The ground near its nest is always clean.'),(14149,767,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Wimpod gather in swarms, constantly on the lookout for danger. They scatter the moment they detect an enemy’s presence.'),(14150,763,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its long, striking legs aren’t just for show but to be used to kick with skill. In victory, it shows off by kicking the defeated, laughing boisterously.'),(14151,763,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A Pokémon known for the beauty of its well-shaped legs, it sometimes appears as a mascot in advertisements for beauty salons.'),(14152,763,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A master of grand and beautiful kicks, it can knock out even kickboxing champions with a single blow.'),(14153,763,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A Pokémon with an aggressive personality and a mastery of kicking, it cackles every time it kicks an opponent.'),(14154,763,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This feared Pokémon has long, slender legs and a cruel heart. It shows no mercy as it stomps on its opponents.'),(14155,763,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','A kick from the hardened tips of this Pokémon’s legs leaves a wound in the opponent’s body and soul that will never heal.'),(14156,771,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It lives in shallow seas, such as areas near a beach. It can eject its internal organs, which it uses to engulf its prey or battle enemies.'),(14157,771,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','These Pokémon line the beaches. The sticky mucous that covers their bodies can be used to soothe sunburned skin. How convenient!'),(14158,771,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The tradition known as Pyukumuku chucking started from the custom of throwing Pyukumuku back into the sea after they wash onshore.'),(14159,771,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its entire body is covered in its own slime. If you accidentally step on one, you’ll slip, and it will get mad and smack you!'),(14160,771,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It lives in warm, shallow waters. If it encounters a foe, it will spit out its internal organs as a means to punch them.'),(14161,771,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s covered in a slime that keeps its skin moist, allowing it to stay on land for days without drying up.'),(14162,765,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Known for its extreme intelligence, this Pokémon will look down on inexperienced Trainers, so it’s best suited to veteran Trainers.'),(14163,765,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Deep in the jungle, high in the lofty canopy, this Pokémon abides. On rare occasions, it shows up at the beach to match wits with Slowking.'),(14164,765,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It normally spends its time meditating in the treetops. It throws Poké Balls and gives other Pokémon orders as it pleases.'),(14165,765,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Oranguru don’t get along with each other, so they’re always engaging in battles of wits to decide which one is superior.'),(14166,765,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','With waves of its fan—made from leaves and its own fur—Oranguru skillfully gives instructions to other Pokémon.'),(14167,765,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It knows the forest inside and out. If it comes across a wounded Pokémon, Oranguru will gather medicinal herbs to treat it.'),(14168,766,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','They form groups of roughly 20 individuals. Their mutual bond is remarkable—they will never let down a comrade.'),(14169,766,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','They battle with hard berries for weapons. Their techniques are passed from the boss to the group, generation upon generation.'),(14170,766,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','They use their saliva to stick leaves to their shoulders. You can tell what troop they belong to from the position of the leaves.'),(14171,766,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Berries are its weapons as well as the staple of its diet. The one that can throw a berry the farthest is the boss of the troop.'),(14172,766,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Displaying amazing teamwork, they follow the orders of their boss as they all help out in the search for their favorite berries.'),(14173,766,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Passimian live in groups of about 20, with each member performing an assigned role. Through cooperation, the group survives.'),(14174,756,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Forests where Shiinotic live are treacherous to enter at night. People confused by its strange lights can never find their way home again.'),(14175,756,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It emits flickering spores that cause drowsiness. When its prey succumb to sleep, this Pokémon feeds on them by sucking in their energy.'),(14176,756,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It puts its prey to sleep and siphons off their vitality through the tip of its arms. If one of its kind is weakened, it helps by sending it vitality.'),(14177,756,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When it starts fighting for territory with Parasect, the entire area gets completely coated in spores!'),(14178,756,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its flickering spores lure in prey and put them to sleep. Once this Pokémon has its prey snoozing, it drains their vitality with its fingertips.'),(14179,756,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If you see a light deep in a forest at night, don’t go near. Shiinotic will make you fall fast asleep.'),(14180,772,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The heavy control mask it wears suppresses its intrinsic capabilities. This Pokémon has some hidden special power.'),(14181,772,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Due to the danger that this synthetic Pokémon may go on a rampage, it wears a control mask to restrain its power.'),(14182,772,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A Pokémon weapon developed for a specific mission, it went berserk during an experiment, so it was cryogenically frozen.'),(14183,772,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','There’s danger of its going on a rampage, so its true power is sealed away beneath its control mask.'),(14184,772,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Rumor has it that the theft of top-secret research notes led to a new instance of this Pokémon being created in the Galar region.'),(14185,772,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It was modeled after a mighty Pokémon of myth. The mask placed upon it limits its power in order to keep it under control.'),(14186,775,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It is born asleep, and it dies asleep. All its movements are apparently no more than the results of it tossing and turning in its dreams.'),(14187,775,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The log it holds was given to it by its parents at birth. It has also been known to cling to the arm of a friendly Trainer.'),(14188,775,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It stays asleep from the moment it’s born. When it falls into a deep sleep, it stops moving altogether.'),(14189,775,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It remains asleep from birth to death as a result of the sedative properties of the leaves that form its diet.'),(14190,774,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Originally making its home in the ozone layer, it hurtles to the ground when the shell enclosing its body grows too heavy.'),(14191,774,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Strong impacts can knock it out of its shell. This Pokémon was born from mutated nanoparticles.'),(14192,774,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It lives in the ozone layer, where it becomes food for stronger Pokémon. When it tries to run away, it falls to the ground.'),(14193,774,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although its outer shell is uncommonly durable, the shock of falling to the ground smashes the shell to smithereens.'),(14194,773,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its trust in its partner is what awakens it. This Pokémon is capable of changing its type, a flexibility that is well displayed in battle.'),(14195,773,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although its name was Type: Null at first, the boy who evolved it into this form gave it the name by which it is now known.'),(14196,773,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This is its form once it has awakened and evolved. Freed from its heavy mask, its speed is greatly increased.'),(14197,773,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Through the bond it formed with its Trainer, its will was strengthened, and it was able to destroy its control mask.'),(14198,773,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A solid bond of trust between this Pokémon and its Trainer awakened the strength hidden within Silvally. It can change its type at will.'),(14199,773,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The final factor needed to release this Pokémon’s true power was a strong bond with a Trainer it trusts.'),(14200,780,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It has a compassionate personality, but if it is angered, it completely destroys its surroundings with its intense breath.'),(14201,780,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon is friendly to people and loves children most of all. It comes from deep in the mountains to play with children it likes in town.'),(14202,780,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','If a child it has made friends with is bullied, Drampa will find the bully’s house and burn it to the ground.'),(14203,780,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It appears in towns and plays with the children. Drampa will protect kids when they’re in danger, so their moms don’t have to worry.'),(14204,780,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The mountains it calls home are nearly two miles in height. On rare occasions, it descends to play with the children living in the towns below.'),(14205,780,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Drampa is a kind and friendly Pokémon—up until it’s angered. When that happens, it stirs up a gale and flattens everything around.'),(14206,785,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This guardian deity of Melemele is brimming with curiosity. It summons thunderclouds and stores their lightning inside its body.'),(14207,785,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It confuses its enemies by flying too quickly for the eye to follow. It has a hair-trigger temper but forgets what made it angry an instant later.'),(14208,785,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s called a guardian deity, if a person or Pokémon puts it in a bad mood, it will become a malevolent deity and attack.'),(14209,785,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The lightning-wielding guardian deity of Melemele, Tapu Koko is brimming with curiosity and appears before people from time to time.'),(14210,784,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it spots enemies, it threatens them by jingling the scales on its tail. Weak opponents will crack and flee in panic.'),(14211,784,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its rigid scales function as offense and defense. In the past, its scales were processed and used to make weapons and other commodities.'),(14212,784,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it howls after finishing off its prey, the metallic sounds of its celebrating comrades can be heard from all around.'),(14213,784,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It battles valiantly with its fists, which are armored in steel scales. Kommo-o specializes in uppercuts.'),(14214,784,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It clatters its tail scales to unnerve opponents. This Pokémon will battle only those who stand steadfast in the face of this display.'),(14215,784,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Certain ruins have paintings of ancient warriors wearing armor made of Kommo-o scales.'),(14216,782,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It expresses its feelings by smacking its scales. Metallic sounds echo through the tall mountains where Jangmo-o lives.'),(14217,782,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','They live in mountains where no trace of humans can be detected. Jangmo-o grow little by little as they battle one another.'),(14218,782,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It smacks the scales on its head against rocks or against the ground to frighten its opponents. It can also contact its friends with these noises.'),(14219,782,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It will never show an enemy its back in battle. Ancient warriors liked Jangmo-o for its valiant disposition and made it one of their own.'),(14220,782,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','They learn to fight by smashing their head scales together. The dueling strengthens both their skills and their spirits.'),(14221,782,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Jangmo-o strikes its scales to communicate with others of its kind. Its scales are actually fur that’s become as hard as metal.'),(14222,778,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its actual appearance is unknown. A scholar who saw what was under its rag was overwhelmed by terror and died from the shock.'),(14223,778,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A lonely Pokémon, it conceals its terrifying appearance beneath an old rag so it can get closer to people and other Pokémon.'),(14224,778,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s a quiet, lonely Pokémon, if you try to look at what’s under its rag, it will become agitated and resist violently.'),(14225,778,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A gust of wind revealed what hides under this Pokémon’s rag to a passing Trainer, who went home and died painfully that very night.'),(14226,778,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It wears a rag fashioned into a Pikachu costume in an effort to look less scary. Unfortunately, the costume only makes it creepier.'),(14227,778,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','There was a scientist who peeked under Mimikyu’s old rag in the name of research. The scientist died of a mysterious disease.'),(14228,786,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This guardian deity of Akala is guilelessly cruel. The fragrant aroma of flowers is the source of its energy.'),(14229,786,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','As it flutters about, it scatters its strangely glowing scales. Touching them is said to restore good health on the spot.'),(14230,786,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It heals the wounds of people and Pokémon by sprinkling them with its sparkling scales. This guardian deity is worshiped on Akala.'),(14231,786,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although called a guardian deity, Tapu Lele is devoid of guilt about its cruel disposition and can be described as nature incarnate.'),(14232,781,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Swinging its massive anchor, it can KO Wailord in a single blow. What appears to be green seaweed is actually its body.'),(14233,781,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The soul of seaweed adrift in the waves became reborn as this Pokémon. It maintains itself with new infusions of seabed detritus and seaweed.'),(14234,781,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It wraps its prey in green seaweed and sucks away their vitality. It only likes to go after big prey like Wailord.'),(14235,781,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its chain-like green seaweed can stretch outward for hundreds of yards. For some reason, it gets along well with Skrelp.'),(14236,781,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','After a piece of seaweed merged with debris from a sunken ship, it was reborn as this ghost Pokémon.'),(14237,781,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','After lowering its anchor, it waits for its prey. It catches large Wailord and drains their life-force.'),(14238,779,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it unleashes its psychic power from the protuberance on its head, the grating sound of grinding teeth echoes through the area.'),(14239,779,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It stuns its prey with psychokinesis and then grinds them to mush with its strong teeth. Even Shellder’s shell is no match for it.'),(14240,779,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It burrows beneath the sand, radiating psychic power from the protuberance on its head. It waits for prey as it surveys the area.'),(14241,779,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its skin is thick enough to fend off Mareanie’s spikes. With its robust teeth, Bruxish crunches up the spikes and eats them.'),(14242,787,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It pulls large trees up by the roots and swings them around. It causes vegetation to grow, and then it absorbs energy from the growth.'),(14243,787,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The guardian deity of Ula’ula is a lazy Pokémon. It commands plants to immobilize its foes and then deals them a savage blow with its horns.'),(14244,787,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s called a guardian deity, it’s violent enough to crush anyone it sees as an enemy.'),(14245,787,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It makes ringing sounds with its tail to let others know where it is, avoiding unneeded conflicts. This guardian deity of Ula’ula controls plants.'),(14246,791,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It is said to live in another world. The intense light it radiates from the surface of its body can make the darkest of nights light up like midday.'),(14247,791,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','This Pokémon is said to be a male evolution of Cosmog. At the activation of its third eye, it departs for another world.'),(14248,791,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Sometimes the result of its opening an Ultra Wormhole is that energy and life-forms from other worlds are called here to this world.'),(14249,791,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','In writings from the distant past, it’s called by the name “the beast that devours the sun.”'),(14250,791,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When light radiates from its body, this Pokémon could almost appear to be the sun. It will dispel any darkness and light up the world.'),(14251,791,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Solgaleo was once known as the Beast That Devours the Sun. Energy in the form of light radiates boundlessly from it.'),(14252,790,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Motionless as if dead, its body is faintly warm to the touch. In the distant past, it was called the cocoon of the stars.'),(14253,790,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','There’s something accumulating around the black core within its hard shell. People think this Pokémon may come from another world.'),(14254,790,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The king who ruled Alola in times of antiquity called it the “cocoon of the stars” and built an altar to worship it.'),(14255,790,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','As it absorbs light, Cosmoem continues to grow. Its golden shell is surprisingly solid.'),(14256,790,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The absorption of starlight fuels this Pokémon’s growth. The shell that encases it is harder than any known material.'),(14257,790,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It sucks in dust from the air at an astounding rate, frantically building up energy within its core as preparation for evolution.'),(14258,789,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Its body is gaseous and frail. It slowly grows as it collects dust from the atmosphere.'),(14259,789,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','In ages past, it was called the child of the stars. It’s said to be a Pokémon from another world, but no specific details are known.'),(14260,789,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Even though its helpless, gaseous body can be blown away by the slightest breeze, it doesn’t seem to care.'),(14261,789,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Whether or not it’s a Pokémon from this world is a mystery. When it’s in a jam, it warps away to a safe place to hide.'),(14262,789,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon came from another universe. Its gaseous body is so light that even a gentle breeze can blow it away.'),(14263,789,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Cosmog is very curious but not very cautious, often placing itself in danger. If things start to look dicey, it teleports away.'),(14264,792,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It is said to be a female evolution of Cosmog. When its third eye activates, away it flies to another world.'),(14265,792,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Said to live in another world, this Pokémon devours light, drawing the moonless dark veil of night over the brightness of day.'),(14266,792,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Records of it exist in writings from long, long ago, where it was known by the name “the beast that calls the moon.”'),(14267,792,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It sometimes summons unknown powers and life-forms here to this world from holes that lead to other worlds.'),(14268,792,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Known as the Beast That Calls the Moon, this Pokémon lives by taking in any and all light and converting it into its own energy.'),(14269,792,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It steals the light from its surroundings and then becomes the full moon, showering its own light across the night sky.'),(14270,788,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The dense fog it creates brings the downfall and destruction of its confused enemies. Ocean currents are the source of its energy.'),(14271,788,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The guardian deity of Poni, it can control water. People say it can create pure water that will wash away any uncleanness.'),(14272,788,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This guardian deity of Poni Island manipulates water. Because it lives deep within a thick fog, it came to be both feared and revered.'),(14273,788,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s called a guardian deity, terrible calamities sometimes befall those who recklessly approach Tapu Fini.'),(14274,795,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','One of the dangerous Ultra Beasts, it has been spotted running across the land at terrific speeds.'),(14275,795,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','One of the Ultra Beasts. It refuses to touch anything, perhaps because it senses some uncleanness in this world.'),(14276,795,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A life-form that lives in another world, its body is thin and supple, but it also possesses great power.'),(14277,795,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s alien to this world and a danger here, it’s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),(14278,793,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','One of several mysterious Ultra Beasts. People on the street report observing those infested by it suddenly becoming violent.'),(14279,793,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','One of the Ultra Beasts. It’s unclear whether or not this Pokémon is sentient, but sometimes it can be observed behaving like a young girl.'),(14280,793,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','A life-form from another world, it was dubbed a UB and is thought to produce a strong neurotoxin.'),(14281,793,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It appeared in this world from an Ultra Wormhole. Nihilego appears to be a parasite that lives by feeding on people and Pokémon.'),(14282,794,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Ultra Beast appeared from another world. It shows off its body, but whether that display is a boast or a threat remains unclear.'),(14283,794,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A mysterious life-form called an Ultra Beast. Witnesses saw it pulverize a dump truck with a single punch.'),(14284,794,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s alien to this world and a danger here, it’s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),(14285,794,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Buzzwole goes around showing off its abnormally swollen muscles. It is one kind of Ultra Beast.'),(14286,783,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It leaps at its prey with a courageous shout. Its scaly punches tear its opponents to shreds.'),(14287,783,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It sheds and regrows its scales on a continuous basis. The scales become harder and sharper each time they’re regrown.'),(14288,783,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It makes noise by clanging its scales together. When the rhythm has reached its peak, Hakamo-o attacks.'),(14289,783,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The scales it sheds can be molded and processed to make pots and pans. They conduct heat well, so they’re a popular item.'),(14290,783,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The scaleless, scarred parts of its body are signs of its strength. It shows them off to defeated opponents.'),(14291,783,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Before attacking its enemies, it clashes its scales together and roars. Its sharp claws shred the opposition.'),(14292,777,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The spiny fur on its back is normally at rest. When this Pokémon becomes agitated, its fur stands on end and stabs into its attackers.'),(14293,777,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','The long hairs on its back act as lightning rods. The bolts of lightning it attracts are stored as energy in its electric sac.'),(14294,777,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','When it’s surprised or agitated, the 14 fur spikes on its back will stand up involuntarily.'),(14295,777,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its capacity to produce electricity is somewhat limited, so it gets charged up by letting lightning strike it!'),(14296,777,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','With the long hairs on its back, this Pokémon takes in electricity from other electric Pokémon. It stores what it absorbs in an electric sac.'),(14297,777,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it’s in trouble, it curls up into a ball, makes its fur spikes stand on end, and then discharges electricity indiscriminately.'),(14298,776,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','The shell on its back is chemically unstable and explodes violently if struck. The hole in its stomach is its weak point.'),(14299,776,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It gushes fire and poisonous gases from its nostrils. Its dung is an explosive substance and can be put to various uses.'),(14300,776,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It lives in volcanoes and eats sulfur and other minerals. Materials from the food it eats form the basis of its explosive shell.'),(14301,776,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its exploding shell poses a real danger but is sensitive to moisture. On rainy days, Turtonator takes silent refuge in caves.'),(14302,776,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Explosive substances coat the shell on its back. Enemies that dare attack it will be blown away by an immense detonation.'),(14303,776,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Eating sulfur in its volcanic habitat is what causes explosive compounds to develop in its shell. Its droppings are also dangerously explosive.'),(14304,797,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. Witnesses observed it flying across the sky at high speed.'),(14305,797,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','One kind of Ultra Beast. Witnesses have seen it burn down a forest by expelling gas from its two arms.'),(14306,797,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','One of the dangerous UBs, high energy readings can be detected coming from both of its huge arms.'),(14307,797,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s alien to this world and a danger here, it’s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),(14308,798,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Ultra Beast came from the Ultra Wormhole. It seems not to attack enemies on its own, but its sharp body is a dangerous weapon in itself.'),(14309,798,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','One of the Ultra Beast life-forms, it was observed cutting down a gigantic steel tower with one stroke of its blade.'),(14310,798,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Ultra Beast’s body, which is as thin as paper, is like a sharpened sword.'),(14311,798,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s alien to this world and a danger here, it’s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),(14312,800,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Reminiscent of the Ultra Beasts, this life-form, apparently asleep underground, is thought to have come from another world in ancient times.'),(14313,800,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Light is apparently the source of its energy. It has an extraordinarily vicious disposition and is constantly firing off laser beams.'),(14314,800,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It looks somehow pained as it rages around in search of light, which serves as its energy. It’s apparently from another world.'),(14315,800,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Light is the source of its energy. If it isn’t devouring light, impurities build up in it and on it, and Necrozma darkens and stops moving.'),(14316,800,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It survives by absorbing light. After a long time spent slumbering underground, impurities accumulated within it, causing its body to darken.'),(14317,800,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It needs light to survive, and it goes on a rampage seeking it out. Its laser beams will cut anything to pieces.'),(14318,799,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It has gobbled mountains and swallowed whole buildings, according to reports. It’s one of the Ultra Beasts.'),(14319,799,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A dangerous Ultra Beast, it appears to be eating constantly, but for some reason its droppings have never been found.'),(14320,799,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s alien to this world and a danger here, it’s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),(14321,799,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','An unknown life-form called a UB. It may be constantly hungry—it is certainly always devouring something.'),(14322,796,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','One of the mysterious life-forms known as Ultra Beasts. Astonishing electric shocks emanate from its entire body, according to witnesses.'),(14323,796,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. It raided a power plant, so people think it energizes itself with electricity.'),(14324,796,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Although it’s alien to this world and a danger here, it’s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),(14325,796,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','They’ve been dubbed Ultra Beasts. Some of them stand unmoving, like trees, with their arms and legs stuck into the ground.'),(14326,810,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it uses its special stick to strike up a beat, the sound waves produced carry revitalizing energy to the plants and flowers in the area.'),(14327,810,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It attacks with rapid beats of its stick. As it strikes with amazing speed, it gets more and more pumped.'),(14328,808,'lets-go-pikachu','Gen VII (Kanto)','It melts particles of iron and other metals found in the subsoil, so it can absorb them into its body of molten steel.'),(14329,808,'lets-go-eevee','Gen VII (Kanto)','It melts particles of iron and other metals found in the subsoil, so it can absorb them into its body of molten steel.'),(14330,808,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It dissolves and eats metal. Circulating liquid metal within its body is how it generates energy.'),(14331,808,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','They live as a group, but when the time comes, one strong Meltan will absorb all the others and evolve.'),(14332,811,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The faster a Thwackey can beat out a rhythm with its two sticks, the more respect it wins from its peers.'),(14333,811,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it’s drumming out rapid beats in battle, it gets so caught up in the rhythm that it won’t even notice that it’s already knocked out its opponent.'),(14334,802,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','Able to conceal itself in shadows, it never appears before humans, so its very existence was the stuff of myth.'),(14335,802,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It lurks in the shadows of others, copying their movements and powers. This Pokémon is craven and cowering.'),(14336,802,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It slips into the shadows of others and mimics their powers and movements. As it improves, it becomes stronger than those it’s imitating.'),(14337,802,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It sinks into the shadows of people and Pokémon, where it can understand their feelings and copy their capabilities.'),(14338,802,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','By slipping into the shadow of a martial arts master and copying their movements, this Pokémon learned the ultimate techniques.'),(14339,802,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon can conceal itself in any shadow, so it went undiscovered for a long time.'),(14340,809,'lets-go-pikachu','Gen VII (Kanto)','Revered long ago for its capacity to create iron from nothing, for some reason it has come back to life after 3,000 years.'),(14341,809,'lets-go-eevee','Gen VII (Kanto)','Revered long ago for its capacity to create iron from nothing, for some reason it has come back to life after 3,000 years.'),(14342,809,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','At the end of its life-span, Melmetal will rust and fall apart. The small shards left behind will eventually be reborn as Meltan.'),(14343,809,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Centrifugal force is behind the punches of Melmetal’s heavy hex-nut arms. Melmetal is said to deliver the strongest punches of all Pokémon.'),(14344,803,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world.'),(14345,803,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','An Ultra Beast that lives in a different world, it cackles wildly as it sprays its opponents with poison from the needles on its head.'),(14346,804,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It stores hundreds of liters of poisonous liquid inside its body. It is one of the organisms known as UBs.'),(14347,804,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','One kind of Ultra Beast, it fires a glowing, venomous liquid from its needles. This liquid is also immensely adhesive.'),(14348,807,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they’ll be electrocuted by the flying sparks.'),(14349,807,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','It approaches its enemies at the speed of lightning, then tears them limb from limb with its sharp claws.'),(14350,807,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It runs as fast as lightning strikes, shredding its opponents with its high-voltage claws.'),(14351,807,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Electricity sparks from the pads on its limbs. Wherever Zeraora runs, lightning flashes and thunder echoes.'),(14352,812,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','By drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle.'),(14353,812,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The one with the best drumming techniques becomes the boss of the troop. It has a gentle disposition and values harmony among its group.'),(14354,813,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A warm-up of running around gets fire energy coursing through this Pokémon’s body. Once that happens, it’s ready to fight at full power.'),(14355,813,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It has special pads on the backs of its feet, and one on its nose. Once it’s raring to fight, these pads radiate tremendous heat.'),(14356,805,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It appeared from an Ultra Wormhole. Each one appears to be made up of many life-forms stacked one on top of each other.'),(14357,805,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','When stone walls started moving and attacking, the brute’s true identity was this mysterious life-form, which brings to mind an Ultra Beast.'),(14358,806,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It slithers toward people. Then, without warning, it triggers the explosion of its own head. It’s apparently one kind of Ultra Beast.'),(14359,806,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','A UB that appeared from an Ultra Wormhole, it causes explosions, then takes advantage of opponents’ surprise to rob them of their vitality.'),(14360,816,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When scared, this Pokémon cries. Its tears pack the chemical punch of 100 onions, and attackers won’t be able to resist weeping.'),(14361,816,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it gets wet, its skin changes color, and this Pokémon becomes invisible as if it were camouflaged.'),(14362,820,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It stashes berries in its tail—so many berries that they fall out constantly. But this Pokémon is a bit slow-witted, so it doesn’t notice the loss.'),(14363,820,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Common throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon has strong teeth and can chew through the toughest of berry shells.'),(14364,817,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A clever combatant, this Pokémon battles using water balloons created with moisture secreted from its palms.'),(14365,817,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Highly intelligent but also very lazy, it keeps enemies out of its territory by laying traps everywhere.'),(14366,819,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Found throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon becomes uneasy if its cheeks are ever completely empty of berries.'),(14367,819,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It eats berries nonstop—a habit that has made it more resilient than it looks. It’ll show up on farms, searching for yet more berries.'),(14368,814,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its thick and fluffy fur protects it from the cold and enables it to use hotter fire moves.'),(14369,814,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It kicks berries right off the branches of trees and then juggles them with its feet, practicing its footwork.'),(14370,815,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It juggles a pebble with its feet, turning it into a burning soccer ball. Its shots strike opponents hard and leave them scorched.'),(14371,815,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s skilled at both offense and defense, and it gets pumped up when cheered on. But if it starts showboating, it could put itself in a tough spot.'),(14372,818,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It has many hidden capabilities, such as fingertips that can shoot water and a membrane on its back that it can use to glide through the air.'),(14373,818,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its nictitating membranes let it pick out foes’ weak points so it can precisely blast them with water that shoots from its fingertips at Mach 3.'),(14374,822,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Smart enough to use tools in battle, these Pokémon have been seen picking up rocks and flinging them or using ropes to wrap up enemies.'),(14375,822,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The lessons of many harsh battles have taught it how to accurately judge an opponent’s strength.'),(14376,821,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It will bravely challenge any opponent, no matter how powerful. This Pokémon benefits from every battle—even a defeat increases its strength a bit.'),(14377,821,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Jumping nimbly about, this small-bodied Pokémon takes advantage of even the slightest opportunity to disorient larger opponents.'),(14378,825,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It barely moves, but it’s still alive. Hiding in its shell without food or water seems to have awakened its psychic powers.'),(14379,825,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','As it grows inside its shell, it uses its psychic abilities to monitor the outside world and prepare for evolution.'),(14380,801,'sun','Gen VII (Alola)','This artificial Pokémon, constructed more than 500 years ago, can understand human speech but cannot itself speak.'),(14381,801,'moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Its mechanized body is merely a vessel. Its true self is its Soul-Heart, an artificial soul.'),(14382,801,'ultra-sun','Gen VII (Alola)','It synchronizes its consciousness with others to understand their feelings. This faculty makes it useful for taking care of people.'),(14383,801,'ultra-moon','Gen VII (Alola)','Built roughly 500 years ago by a scientist, the part called the Soul-Heart is the actual life-form.'),(14384,824,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A constant collector of information, this Pokémon is very smart. Very strong is what it isn’t.'),(14385,824,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Often found in gardens, this Pokémon has hairs on its body that it uses to assess its surroundings.'),(14386,823,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon reigns supreme in the skies of the Galar region. The black luster of its steel body could drive terror into the heart of any foe.'),(14387,823,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','With their great intellect and flying skills, these Pokémon very successfully act as the Galar region’s airborne taxi service.'),(14388,827,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Aided by the soft pads on its feet, it silently raids the food stores of other Pokémon. It survives off its ill-gotten gains.'),(14389,827,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Cunning and cautious, this Pokémon survives by stealing food from others. It erases its tracks with swipes of its tail as it makes off with its plunder.'),(14390,830,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The seeds attached to its cotton fluff are full of nutrients. It spreads them on the wind so that plants and other Pokémon can benefit from them.'),(14391,830,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The cotton on the head of this Pokémon can be spun into a glossy, gorgeous yarn—a Galar regional specialty.'),(14392,829,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It anchors itself in the ground with its single leg, then basks in the sun. After absorbing enough sunlight, its petals spread as it blooms brilliantly.'),(14393,829,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It whirls around in the wind while singing a joyous song. This delightful display has charmed many into raising this Pokémon.'),(14394,834,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','With jaws that can shear through steel rods, this highly aggressive Pokémon chomps down on its unfortunate prey.'),(14395,834,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon rapidly extends its retractable neck to sink its sharp fangs into distant enemies and take them down.'),(14396,832,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Weave a carpet from its springy wool, and you end up with something closer to a trampoline. You’ll start to bounce the moment you set foot on it.'),(14397,832,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its majestic horns are meant only to impress the opposite gender. They never see use in battle.'),(14398,835,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon is very popular as a herding dog in the Galar region. As it runs, it generates electricity from the base of its tail.'),(14399,835,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This gluttonous Pokémon only assists people with their work because it wants treats. As it runs, it crackles with electricity.'),(14400,828,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It secretly marks potential targets with a scent. By following the scent, it stalks its targets and steals from them when they least expect it.'),(14401,828,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','With a lithe body and sharp claws, it goes around stealing food and eggs. Boltund is its natural enemy.'),(14402,826,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s famous for its high level of intelligence, and the large size of its brain is proof that it also possesses immense psychic power.'),(14403,826,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It emits psychic energy to observe and study what’s around it—and what’s around it can include things over six miles away.'),(14404,833,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Apparently the itch of its teething impels it to snap its jaws at anything in front of it.'),(14405,833,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It starts off battles by attacking with its rock-hard horn, but as soon as the opponent flinches, this Pokémon bites down and never lets go.'),(14406,838,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It forms coal inside its body. Coal dropped by this Pokémon once helped fuel the lives of people in the Galar region.'),(14407,838,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','By rapidly rolling its legs, it can travel at over 18 mph. The temperature of the flames it breathes exceeds 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit.'),(14408,836,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon generates electricity and channels it into its legs to keep them going strong. Boltund can run nonstop for three full days.'),(14409,836,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It sends electricity through its legs to boost their strength. Running at top speed, it easily breaks 50 mph.'),(14410,837,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Most of its body has the same composition as coal. Fittingly, this Pokémon was first discovered in coal mines about 400 years ago.'),(14411,837,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It can race around like a unicycle, even on rough, rocky terrain. Burning coal sustains it.'),(14412,839,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s usually peaceful, but the vandalism of mines enrages it. Offenders will be incinerated with flames that reach 2,700 degrees Fahrenheit.'),(14413,839,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','While it’s engaged in battle, its mountain of coal will burn bright red, sending off sparks that scorch the surrounding area.'),(14414,840,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It spends its entire life inside an apple. It hides from its natural enemies, bird Pokémon, by pretending it’s just an apple and nothing more.'),(14415,840,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','As soon as it’s born, it burrows into an apple. Not only does the apple serve as its food source, but the flavor of the fruit determines its evolution.'),(14416,842,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Eating a sweet apple caused its evolution. A nectarous scent wafts from its body, luring in the bug Pokémon it preys on.'),(14417,842,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its body is covered in sweet nectar, and the skin on its back is especially yummy. Children used to have it as a snack.'),(14418,844,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it contracts its body, over 220 pounds of sand sprays from its nose. If it ever runs out of sand, it becomes disheartened.'),(14419,844,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its unique style of coiling allows it to blast sand out of its sand sac more efficiently.'),(14420,843,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','As it digs, it swallows sand and stores it in its neck pouch. The pouch can hold more than 17 pounds of sand.'),(14421,843,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It spews sand from its nostrils. While the enemy is blinded, it burrows into the ground to hide.'),(14422,841,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It ate a sour apple, and that induced its evolution. In its cheeks, it stores an acid capable of causing chemical burns.'),(14423,841,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It flies on wings of apple skin and spits a powerful acid. It can also change its shape into that of an apple.'),(14424,845,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s so strong that it can knock out some opponents in a single hit, but it also may forget what it’s battling midfight.'),(14425,845,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This hungry Pokémon swallows Arrokuda whole. Occasionally, it makes a mistake and tries to swallow a Pokémon other than its preferred prey.'),(14426,847,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon has a jaw that’s as sharp as a spear and as strong as steel. Apparently Barraskewda’s flesh is surprisingly tasty, too.'),(14427,847,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It spins its tail fins to propel itself, surging forward at speeds of over 100 knots before ramming prey and spearing into them.'),(14428,850,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It stores flammable gas in its body and uses it to generate heat. The yellow sections on its belly get particularly hot.'),(14429,850,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It wraps prey up with its heated body, cooking them in its coils. Once they’re well-done, it will voraciously nibble them down to the last morsel.'),(14430,831,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its curly fleece is such an effective cushion that this Pokémon could fall off a cliff and stand right back up at the bottom, unharmed.'),(14431,831,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If its fleece grows too long, Wooloo won’t be able to move. Cloth made with the wool of this Pokémon is surprisingly strong.'),(14432,849,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When this Pokémon sounds as if it’s strumming a guitar, it’s actually clawing at the protrusions on its chest to generate electricity.'),(14433,849,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This short-tempered and aggressive Pokémon chugs stagnant water to absorb any toxins it might contain.'),(14434,848,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It stores poison in an internal poison sac and secretes that poison through its skin. If you touch this Pokémon, a tingling sensation follows.'),(14435,848,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It manipulates the chemical makeup of its poison to produce electricity. The voltage is weak, but it can cause a tingling paralysis.'),(14436,846,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','If it sees any movement around it, this Pokémon charges for it straightaway, leading with its sharply pointed jaw. It’s very proud of that jaw.'),(14437,846,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','After it’s eaten its fill, its movements become extremely sluggish. That’s when Cramorant swallows it up.'),(14438,856,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Via the protrusion on its head, it senses other creatures’ emotions. If you don’t have a calm disposition, it will never warm up to you.'),(14439,856,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If this Pokémon senses a strong emotion, it will run away as fast as it can. It prefers areas without people.'),(14440,853,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A body made up of nothing but muscle makes the grappling moves this Pokémon performs with its tentacles tremendously powerful.'),(14441,853,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Searching for an opponent to test its skills against, it emerges onto land. Once the battle is over, it returns to the sea.'),(14442,857,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','No matter who you are, if you bring strong emotions near this Pokémon, it will silence you violently.'),(14443,857,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Using the braids on its head, it pummels foes to get them to quiet down. One blow from those braids would knock out a professional boxer.'),(14444,851,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it heats up, its body temperature reaches about 1,500 degrees Fahrenheit. It lashes its body like a whip and launches itself at enemies.'),(14445,851,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','While its burning body is already dangerous on its own, this excessively hostile Pokémon also has large and very sharp fangs.'),(14446,855,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This species lives in antique teapots. Most pots are forgeries, but on rare occasions, an authentic work is found.'),(14447,855,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Leaving leftover black tea unattended is asking for this Pokémon to come along and pour itself into it, turning the tea into a new Polteageist.'),(14448,859,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Through its nose, it sucks in the emanations produced by people and Pokémon when they feel annoyed. It thrives off this negative energy.'),(14449,859,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It sneaks into people’s homes, stealing things and feasting on the negative energy of the frustrated occupants.'),(14450,854,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon is said to have been born when a lonely spirit possessed a cold, leftover cup of tea.'),(14451,854,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The teacup in which this Pokémon makes its home is a famous piece of antique tableware. Many forgeries are in circulation.'),(14452,852,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s very curious, but its means of investigating things is to try to punch them with its tentacles. The search for food is what brings it onto land.'),(14453,852,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its tentacles tear off easily, but it isn’t alarmed when that happens—it knows they’ll grow back. It’s about as smart as a three-year-old.'),(14454,858,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It emits psychic power strong enough to cause headaches as a deterrent to the approach of others.'),(14455,858,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If you’re too loud around it, you risk being torn apart by the claws on its tentacle. This Pokémon is also known as the Forest Witch.'),(14456,860,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it gets down on all fours as if to beg for forgiveness, it’s trying to lure opponents in so that it can stab them with its spear-like hair.'),(14457,860,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','With sly cunning, it tries to lure people into the woods. Some believe it to have the power to make crops grow.'),(14458,863,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','What appears to be an iron helmet is actually hardened hair. This Pokémon lives for the thrill of battle.'),(14459,863,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','After many battles, it evolved dangerous claws that come together to form daggers when extended.'),(14460,861,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','With the hair wrapped around its body helping to enhance its muscles, this Pokémon can overwhelm even Machamp.'),(14461,861,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its hairs work like muscle fibers. When its hairs unfurl, they latch on to opponents, ensnaring them as tentacles would.'),(14462,864,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its shell is overflowing with its heightened otherworldly energy. The ectoplasm serves as protection for this Pokémon’s core spirit.'),(14463,864,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Be cautious of the ectoplasmic body surrounding its soul. You’ll become stiff as stone if you touch it.'),(14464,866,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s highly skilled at tap-dancing. It waves its cane of ice in time with its graceful movements.'),(14465,866,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its amusing movements make it very popular. It releases its psychic power from the pattern on its belly.'),(14466,870,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Five of them are troopers, and one is the brass. The brass’s orders are absolute.'),(14467,870,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The six of them work together as one Pokémon. Teamwork is also their battle strategy, and they constantly change their formation as they fight.'),(14468,865,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Only Farfetch’d that have survived many battles can attain this evolution. When this Pokémon’s leek withers, it will retire from combat.'),(14469,865,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','After deflecting attacks with its hard leaf shield, it strikes back with its sharp leek stalk. The leek stalk is both weapon and food.'),(14470,867,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','A powerful curse was woven into an ancient painting. After absorbing the spirit of a Yamask, the painting began to move.'),(14471,867,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Never touch its shadowlike body, or you’ll be shown the horrific memories behind the picture carved into it.'),(14472,869,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it trusts a Trainer, it will treat them to berries it’s decorated with cream.'),(14473,869,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','When Alcremie is content, the cream it secretes from its hands becomes sweeter and richer.'),(14474,871,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It feeds on seaweed, using its teeth to scrape it off rocks. Electric current flows from the tips of its spines.'),(14475,871,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It stores electricity in each spine. Even if one gets broken off, it still continues to emit electricity for at least three hours.'),(14476,868,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon was born from sweet-smelling particles in the air. Its body is made of cream.'),(14477,868,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','They say that any patisserie visited by Milcery is guaranteed success and good fortune.'),(14478,873,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Icy scales fall from its wings like snow as it flies over fields and mountains. The temperature of its wings is less than −290 degrees Fahrenheit.'),(14479,873,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It shows no mercy to any who desecrate fields and mountains. It will fly around on its icy wings, causing a blizzard to chase offenders away.'),(14480,875,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It drifted in on the flow of ocean waters from a frigid place. It keeps its head iced constantly to make sure it stays nice and cold.'),(14481,875,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon keeps its heat-sensitive head cool with ice. It fishes for its food, dangling its single hair into the sea to lure in prey.'),(14482,862,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its voice is staggering in volume. Obstagoon has a tendency to take on a threatening posture and shout—this move is known as Obstruct.'),(14483,862,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It evolved after experiencing numerous fights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a shout that would make any opponent flinch.'),(14484,872,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It spits out thread imbued with a frigid sort of energy and uses it to tie its body to branches, disguising itself as an icicle while it sleeps.'),(14485,872,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It eats snow that piles up on the ground. The more snow it eats, the bigger and more impressive the spikes on its back grow.'),(14486,874,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It stands in grasslands, watching the sun’s descent from zenith to horizon. This Pokémon has a talent for delivering dynamic kicks.'),(14487,874,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Once a year, on a specific date and at a specific time, they gather out of nowhere and form up in a circle.'),(14488,877,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','As it eats the seeds stored up in its pocket-like pouches, this Pokémon is not just satisfying its constant hunger. It’s also generating electricity.'),(14489,877,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It carries electrically roasted seeds with it as if they’re precious treasures. No matter how much it eats, it always gets hungry again in short order.'),(14490,882,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Powerful legs and jaws made it the apex predator of its time. Its own overhunting of its prey was what drove it to extinction.'),(14491,882,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its mighty legs are capable of running at speeds exceeding 40 mph, but this Pokémon can’t breathe unless it’s underwater.'),(14492,879,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','They came over from another region long ago and worked together with humans. Their green skin is resistant to water.'),(14493,879,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','These Pokémon live in herds. Their trunks have incredible grip strength, strong enough to crush giant rocks into powder.'),(14494,881,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The shaking of its freezing upper half is what generates its electricity. It has a hard time walking around.'),(14495,881,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon lived on prehistoric seashores and was able to preserve food with the ice on its body. It went extinct because it moved so slowly.'),(14496,880,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','In ancient times, it was unbeatable thanks to its powerful lower body, but it went extinct anyway after it depleted all its plant-based food sources.'),(14497,880,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The powerful muscles in its tail generate its electricity. Compared to its lower body, its upper half is entirely too small.'),(14498,883,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Though it’s able to capture prey by freezing its surroundings, it has trouble eating the prey afterward because its mouth is on top of its head.'),(14499,883,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The skin on its face is impervious to attack, but breathing difficulties made this Pokémon go extinct anyway.'),(14500,878,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It digs up the ground with its trunk. It’s also very strong, being able to carry loads of over five tons without any problem at all.'),(14501,878,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If a job requires serious strength, this Pokémon will excel at it. Its copper body tarnishes in the rain, turning a vibrant green color.'),(14502,876,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It uses the horns on its head to sense the emotions of others. Males will act as valets for those they serve, looking after their every need.'),(14503,876,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Through its horns, it can pick up on the emotions of creatures around it. Positive emotions are the source of its strength.'),(14504,884,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its body resembles polished metal, and it’s both lightweight and strong. The only drawback is that it rusts easily.'),(14505,884,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','The special metal that composes its body is very light, so this Pokémon has considerable agility. It lives in caves because it dislikes the rain.'),(14506,886,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It’s capable of flying faster than 120 mph. It battles alongside Dreepy and dotes on them until they successfully evolve.'),(14507,886,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Without a Dreepy to place on its head and care for, it gets so uneasy it’ll try to substitute any Pokémon it finds for the missing Dreepy.'),(14508,893,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Within dense forests, this Pokémon lives in a pack with others of its kind. It’s incredibly aggressive, and the other Pokémon of the forest fear it.'),(14509,893,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Once the vines on Zarude’s body tear off, they become nutrients in the soil. This helps the plants of the forest grow.'),(14510,890,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','The core on its chest absorbs energy emanating from the lands of the Galar region. This energy is what allows Eternatus to stay active.'),(14511,890,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','It was inside a meteorite that fell 20,000 years ago. There seems to be a connection between this Pokémon and the Dynamax phenomenon.'),(14512,888,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Known as a legendary hero, this Pokémon absorbs metal particles, transforming them into a weapon it uses to battle.'),(14513,888,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon has slumbered for many years. Some say it’s Zamazenta’s elder sister—others say the two Pokémon are rivals.'),(14514,891,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Kubfu trains hard to perfect its moves. The moves it masters will determine which form it takes when it evolves.'),(14515,891,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If Kubfu pulls the long white hair on its head, its fighting spirit heightens and power wells up from the depths of its belly.'),(14516,889,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','In times past, it worked together with a king of the people to save the Galar region. It absorbs metal that it then uses in battle.'),(14517,889,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon slept for aeons while in the form of a statue. It was asleep for so long, people forgot that it ever existed.'),(14518,894,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This Pokémon is a cluster of electrical energy. It’s said that removing the rings on Regieleki’s body will unleash the Pokémon’s latent power.'),(14519,894,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its entire body is made up of a single organ that generates electrical energy. Regieleki is capable of creating all Galar’s electricity.'),(14520,895,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','An academic theory proposes that Regidrago’s arms were once the head of an ancient dragon Pokémon. The theory remains unproven.'),(14521,895,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Its body is composed of crystallized dragon energy. Regidrago is said to have the powers of every dragon Pokémon.'),(14522,885,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','After being reborn as a ghost Pokémon, Dreepy wanders the areas it used to inhabit back when it was alive in prehistoric seas.'),(14523,885,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','If this weak Pokémon is by itself, a mere child could defeat it. But if Dreepy has friends to help it train, it can evolve and become much stronger.'),(14524,896,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Glastrier emits intense cold from its hooves. It’s also a belligerent Pokémon—anything it wants, it takes by force.'),(14525,896,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Glastrier has tremendous physical strength, and the mask of ice covering its face is 100 times harder than diamond.'),(14526,899,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well and is a highly useful material for winter clothing.'),(14527,898,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','Calyrex is a merciful Pokémon, capable of providing healing and blessings. It reigned over the Galar region in times of yore.'),(14528,898,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Calyrex is known in legend as a king that ruled over Galar in ancient times. It has the power to cause hearts to mend and plants to spring forth.'),(14529,900,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','A violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone. If one should chance upon this Pokémon in the wilds, one\'s only recourse is to flee.'),(14530,897,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','It probes its surroundings with all its senses save one—it doesn’t use its sense of sight. Spectrier’s kicks are said to separate soul from body.'),(14531,897,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','As it dashes through the night, Spectrier absorbs the life-force of sleeping creatures. It craves silence and solitude.'),(14532,887,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','When it isn’t battling, it keeps Dreepy in the holes on its horns. Once a fight starts, it launches the Dreepy like supersonic missiles.'),(14533,887,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Apparently the Dreepy inside Dragapult’s horns eagerly look forward to being launched out at Mach speeds.'),(14534,892,'sword','Gen VIII (Galar)','This form of Urshifu is a strong believer in the one-hit KO. Its strategy is to leap in close to foes and land a devastating blow with a hardened fist.'),(14535,892,'shield','Gen VIII (Galar)','Inhabiting the mountains of a distant region, this Pokémon races across sheer cliffs, training its legs and refining its moves.'),(14536,912,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon migrated to Paldea from distant lands long ago. The gel secreted by its feathers repels water and grime.'),(14537,912,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its strong legs let it easily swim around in even fast-flowing rivers. It likes to keep things tidy and is prone to overthinking things.'),(14538,903,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Because of Sneasler\'s virulent poison and daunting physical prowess, no other species could hope to best it on the frozen highlands. Preferring solitude, this species does not form packs.'),(14539,907,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden beneath its long fur, slamming the hard flower bud against its opponents.'),(14540,907,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The hardness of Floragato’s fur depends on the Pokémon’s mood. When Floragato is prepared to battle, its fur becomes pointed and needle sharp.'),(14541,906,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its fluffy fur is similar in composition to plants. This Pokémon frequently washes its face to keep it from drying out.'),(14542,906,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The sweet scent its body gives off mesmerizes those around it. The scent grows stronger when this Pokémon is in the sun.'),(14543,901,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','I believe it was Hisui\'s swampy terrain that gave Ursaluna its burly physique and newfound capacity to manipulate peat at will.'),(14544,909,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It lies on warm rocks and uses the heat absorbed by its square-shaped scales to create fire energy.'),(14545,909,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its flame sac is small, so energy is always leaking out. This energy is released from the dent atop Fuecoco’s head and flickers to and fro.'),(14546,904,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname ”sea fiend.” It slurps up poison to nourish itself.'),(14547,910,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The combination of Crocalor’s fire energy and overflowing vitality has caused an egg-shaped fireball to appear on the Pokémon’s head.'),(14548,910,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The valve in Crocalor’s flame sac is closely connected to its vocal cords. This Pokémon utters a guttural cry as it spews flames every which way.'),(14549,911,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The fiery bird changes shape when Skeledirge sings. Rumor has it that the bird was born when the fireball on Skeledirge’s head gained a soul.'),(14550,911,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Skeledirge’s gentle singing soothes the souls of all that hear it. It burns its enemies to a crisp with flames of over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit.'),(14551,905,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','When it flies to this land from across the sea, the bitter winter comes to an end. According to legend, this Pokémon\'s love gives rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui.'),(14552,914,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','A single kick from a Quaquaval can send a truck rolling. This Pokémon uses its powerful legs to perform striking dances from far-off lands.'),(14553,914,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Dancing in ways that evoke far-away places, this Pokémon mesmerizes all that see it. Flourishes of its decorative water feathers slice into its foes.'),(14554,917,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The ball of threads wrapped around its body is elastic enough to deflect the scythes of Scyther, this Pokémon’s natural enemy.'),(14555,917,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The thread it secretes from its rear is as strong as wire. The secret behind the thread’s strength is the topic of ongoing research.'),(14556,915,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It searches for food all day. It possesses a keen sense of smell but doesn’t use it for anything other than foraging.'),(14557,915,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon spurns all but the finest of foods. Its body gives off an herblike scent that bug Pokémon detest.'),(14558,919,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has its third set of legs folded up. When it’s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps over 30 feet using the strength of its legs.'),(14559,919,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It’s highly skilled at a fighting style in which it uses its jumping capabilities to dodge incoming attacks while also dealing damage to opponents.'),(14560,913,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','These Pokémon constantly run through shallow waters to train their legs, then compete with each other to see which of them kicks most gracefully.'),(14561,913,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The hardworking Quaxwell observes people and Pokémon from various regions and incorporates their movements into its own dance routines.'),(14562,908,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon uses the reflective fur lining its cape to camouflage the stem of its flower, creating the illusion that the flower is floating.'),(14563,908,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','With skillful misdirection, it rigs foes with pollen-packed flower bombs. Meowscarada sets off the bombs before its foes realize what’s going on.'),(14564,918,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It clings to branches and ceilings using its threads and moves without a sound. It takes out its prey before the prey even notices it.'),(14565,918,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Spidops covers its territory in tough, sticky threads to set up traps for intruders.'),(14566,916,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Oinkologne is proud of its fine, glossy skin. It emits a concentrated scent from the tip of its tail.'),(14567,916,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It entrances female Pokémon with the sweet, alluring scent that wafts from all over its body.'),(14568,920,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When it decides to fight all out, it stands on its previously folded legs to enter Showdown Mode. It neutralizes its enemies in short order.'),(14569,920,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It uses its normally folded third set of legs when in Showdown Mode. This places a huge burden on its body, so it can’t stay in this mode for long.'),(14570,921,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has underdeveloped electric sacs on its cheeks. These sacs can produce electricity only if Pawmi rubs them furiously with the pads on its forepaws.'),(14571,921,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.'),(14572,924,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them.'),(14573,924,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The pair sticks together no matter what. They split any food they find exactly in half and then eat it together.'),(14574,925,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The two little ones just appeared one day. The group might be a family of related Pokémon, but nobody knows for sure.'),(14575,925,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The larger pair protects the little ones during battles. When facing strong opponents, the whole group will join the fight.'),(14576,923,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon normally is slow to react, but once it enters battle, it will strike down its enemies with lightning-fast movements.'),(14577,923,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Pawmot’s fluffy fur acts as a battery. It can store the same amount of electricity as an electric car.'),(14578,902,'legends-arceus','Gen VIII (Hisui)','Clads itself in the souls of comrades that perished before fulfilling their goals of journeying upstream. No other species throughout all Hisui\'s rivers is Basculegion\'s equal.'),(14579,922,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When its group is attacked, Pawmo is the first to leap into battle, defeating enemies with a fighting technique that utilizes electric shocks.'),(14580,922,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Pawmo uses a unique fighting technique in which it uses its forepaws to strike foes and zap them with electricity from its paw pads simultaneously.'),(14581,929,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Dolliv shares its tasty, fresh-scented oil with others. This species has coexisted with humans since times long gone.'),(14582,929,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It basks in the sun to its heart’s content until the fruits on its head ripen. After that, Dolliv departs from human settlements and goes on a journey.'),(14583,934,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Garganacl will rub its fingertips together and sprinkle injured Pokémon with salt. Even severe wounds will promptly heal afterward.'),(14584,934,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Many Pokémon gather around Garganacl, hoping to lick at its mineral-rich salt.'),(14585,933,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon dry cures its prey by spraying salt over them. The curing process steals away the water in the prey’s body.'),(14586,933,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It compresses rock salt inside its body and shoots out hardened salt pellets with enough force to perforate an iron sheet.'),(14587,928,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It protects itself from enemies by emitting oil from the fruit on its head. This oil is bitter and astringent enough to make someone flinch.'),(14588,928,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon converts nutrients into oil, which it stores in the fruit on its head. It can easily go a whole week without eating or drinking.'),(14589,926,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon is smooth and moist to the touch. Yeast in Fidough’s breath induces fermentation in the Pokémon’s vicinity.'),(14590,926,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The yeast in Fidough’s breath is useful for cooking, so this Pokémon has been protected by people since long ago.'),(14591,935,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents.'),(14592,935,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its firepower increases when it fights, reaching over 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit. It likes berries that are rich in fat.'),(14593,936,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.'),(14594,936,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon clads itself in armor that has been fortified by psychic and fire energy, and it shoots blazing fireballs.'),(14595,930,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This calm Pokémon is very compassionate. It will share its delicious, nutrient-rich oil with weakened Pokémon.'),(14596,930,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon drives back enemies by launching its rich, aromatic oil at them with enough force to smash a boulder.'),(14597,927,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The pleasant aroma that emanates from this Pokémon’s body helps wheat grow, so Dachsbun has been treasured by farming villages.'),(14598,927,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The surface of this Pokémon’s skin hardens when exposed to intense heat, and its body has an appetizing aroma.'),(14599,931,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','These Pokémon prefer to live in cities. They form flocks based on the color of their feathers, and they fight over territory.'),(14600,931,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Green-feathered flocks hold the most sway. When they’re out searching for food in the mornings and evenings, it gets very noisy.'),(14601,932,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt.'),(14602,932,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The ground scrapes its body as it travels, causing it to leave salt behind. Salt is constantly being created and replenished inside Nacli’s body.'),(14603,937,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The fiery blades on its arms burn fiercely with the lingering resentment of a sword wielder who fell before accomplishing their goal.'),(14604,937,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','An old set of armor steeped in grudges caused this Pokémon’s evolution. Ceruledge cuts its enemies to pieces without mercy.'),(14605,941,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to amplify its electricity. By riding the wind, this Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day.'),(14606,941,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It uses its throat sac to store electricity generated by its wings. There’s hardly any oil in its feathers, so it is a poor swimmer.'),(14607,938,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate electricity. If it senses danger, it will make its head blink on and off to alert its allies.'),(14608,938,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It floats using the electricity stored in its body. When thunderclouds are around, Tadbulb will float higher off the ground.'),(14609,939,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When this Pokémon expands and contracts its wobbly body, the belly-button dynamo in its stomach produces a huge amount of electricity.'),(14610,939,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','What appear to be eyeballs are actually organs for discharging the electricity generated by Bellibolt’s belly-button dynamo.'),(14611,940,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When its wings catch the wind, the bones within produce electricity. This Pokémon dives into the ocean, catching prey by electrocuting them.'),(14612,940,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','These Pokémon make their nests on coastal cliffs. The nests have a strange, crackling texture, and they’re a popular delicacy.'),(14613,945,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The color of the poisonous saliva depends on what the Pokémon eats. Grafaiai covers its fingers in its saliva and draws patterns on trees in forests.'),(14614,945,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Each Grafaiai paints its own individual pattern, and it will paint that same pattern over and over again throughout its life.'),(14615,943,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon can store energy in its large dewlap. Mabosstiff unleashes this energy all at once to blow away enemies.'),(14616,943,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Mabosstiff loves playing with children. Though usually gentle, it takes on an intimidating look when protecting its family.'),(14617,944,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire.'),(14618,944,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','To keep enemies away from its territory, it paints markings around its nest using a poisonous liquid that has an acrid odor.'),(14619,942,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It always scowls in an attempt to make opponents take it seriously, but even crying children will burst into laughter when they see Maschiff’s face.'),(14620,942,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its well-developed jaw and fangs are strong enough to crunch through boulders, and its thick fat makes for an excellent defense.'),(14621,946,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','A soul unable to move on to the afterlife was blown around by the wind until it got tangled up with dried grass and became a Pokémon.'),(14622,946,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Not even Bramblin knows where it is headed as it tumbles across the wilderness, blown by the wind. It loathes getting wet.'),(14623,947,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It will open the branches of its head to envelop its prey. Once it absorbs all the life energy it needs, it expels the prey and discards it.'),(14624,947,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Brambleghast wanders around arid regions. On rare occasions, mass outbreaks of these Pokémon will bury an entire town.'),(14625,950,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Klawf hangs upside-down from cliffs, waiting for prey. But Klawf can’t remain in this position for long because its blood rushes to its head.'),(14626,950,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon lives on sheer cliffs. It sidesteps opponents’ attacks, then lunges for their weak spots with its claws.'),(14627,948,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Toedscool lives in muggy forests. The flaps that fall from its body are chewy and very delicious.'),(14628,948,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Though it looks like Tentacool, Toedscool is a completely different species. Its legs may be thin, but it can run at a speed of 30 mph.'),(14629,949,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','These Pokémon gather into groups and form colonies deep within forests. They absolutely hate it when strangers approach.'),(14630,949,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It coils its 10 tentacles around prey and sucks out their nutrients, causing the prey pain. The folds along the rim of its head are a popular delicacy.'),(14631,960,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.'),(14632,960,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Though it looks like Diglett, Wiglett is an entirely different species. The resemblance seems to be a coincidental result of environmental adaptation.'),(14633,951,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in, the more spicy chemicals are produced by its body, and thus the spicier its moves become.'),(14634,951,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Traditional Paldean dishes can be extremely spicy because they include the shed front teeth of Capsakid among their ingredients.'),(14635,957,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.'),(14636,957,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon pounds iron scraps together to make a hammer. It will remake the hammer again and again until it’s satisfied with the result.'),(14637,952,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The red head converts spicy chemicals into fire energy and blasts the surrounding area with a super spicy stream of flame.'),(14638,952,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The green head has turned vicious due to the spicy chemicals stimulating its brain. Once it goes on a rampage, there is no stopping it.'),(14639,955,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Flittle’s toes levitate about half an inch above the ground because of the psychic power emitted from the frills on the Pokémon’s belly.'),(14640,955,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It spends its time running around wastelands. If anyone steals its beloved berries, it will chase them down and exact its revenge.'),(14641,958,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer.'),(14642,958,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','These Pokémon make their homes in piles of scrap metal. They test the strength of each other’s hammers by smashing them together.'),(14643,953,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon creates a mud ball by mixing sand and dirt with psychic energy. It treasures its mud ball more than its own life.'),(14644,953,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It rolls its mud ball around while the energy it needs for evolution matures. Eventually the time comes for it to evolve.'),(14645,954,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The body that supports the ball barely moves. Therefore, it is thought that the true body of this Pokémon is actually inside the ball.'),(14646,954,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','An infant sleeps inside the ball. Rabsca rolls the ball soothingly with its legs to ensure the infant sleeps comfortably.'),(14647,956,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It immobilizes opponents by bathing them in psychic power from its large eyes. Despite its appearance, it has a vicious temperament.'),(14648,956,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It emits psychic power from the gaps between its multicolored frills and sprints at speeds greater than 120 mph.'),(14649,959,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring disposition. It knocks rocks into the sky with its hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight.'),(14650,959,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The hammer tops 220 pounds, yet it gets swung around easily by Tinkaton as it steals whatever it pleases and carries its plunder back home.'),(14651,961,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.'),(14652,961,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','A variety of fish Pokémon, Wugtrio was once considered to be a regional form of Dugtrio.'),(14653,962,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It gathers things up in an apron made from shed feathers added to the Pokémon’s chest feathers, then drops those things from high places for fun.'),(14654,962,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Bombirdier uses the apron on its chest to bundle up food, which it carries back to its nest. It enjoys dropping things that make loud noises.'),(14655,963,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures.'),(14656,963,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its water ring is made from seawater mixed with a sticky fluid that Finizen secretes from its blowhole.'),(14657,966,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It creates a gas out of poison and minerals from rocks. It then detonates the gas in its cylinders—now numbering eight—to generate energy.'),(14658,966,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Revavroom viciously threatens others with the sound of its exhaust. It sticks its tongue out from its cylindrical mouth and sprays toxic fluids.'),(14659,965,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It is said that this Pokémon was born when an unknown poison Pokémon entered and inspirited an engine left at a scrap-processing factory.'),(14660,965,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The steel section is Varoom’s actual body. This Pokémon clings to rocks and converts the minerals within into energy to fuel its activities.'),(14661,964,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon changes its appearance if it hears its allies calling for help. Palafin will never show anybody its moment of transformation.'),(14662,964,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its physical capabilities are no different than a Finizen’s, but when its allies are in danger, it transforms and powers itself up.'),(14663,971,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It is said that a dog Pokémon that died in the wild without ever interacting with a human was reborn as this Pokémon.'),(14664,971,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This friendly Pokémon doesn’t like being alone. Pay it even the slightest bit of attention, and it will follow you forever.'),(14665,969,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It absorbs nutrients from cave walls. The petals it wears are made of crystallized poison.'),(14666,969,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Glimmet’s toxic mineral crystals look just like flower petals. This Pokémon scatters poisonous powder like pollen to protect itself.'),(14667,968,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When attacked, this Pokémon will wield the tendrils on its body like fists and pelt the opponent with a storm of punches.'),(14668,968,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon lives in arid deserts. It maintains its metal body by consuming iron from the soil.'),(14669,967,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Apparently Cyclizar has been allowing people to ride on its back since ancient times. Depictions of this have been found in 10,000-year-old murals.'),(14670,967,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It can sprint at over 70 mph while carrying a human. The rider’s body heat warms Cyclizar’s back and lifts the Pokémon’s spirit.'),(14671,970,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When this Pokémon detects danger, it will open up its crystalline petals and fire beams from its conical body.'),(14672,970,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Glimmora’s petals are made of crystallized poison energy. It has recently become evident that these petals resemble Tera Jewels.'),(14673,972,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Houndstone spends most of its time sleeping in graveyards. Among all the dog Pokémon, this one is most loyal to its master.'),(14674,972,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','A lovingly mourned Pokémon was reborn as Houndstone. It doesn’t like anyone touching the protuberance atop its head.'),(14675,975,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon wanders around snowy, icy areas. It protects its body with powerful muscles and a thick layer of fat under its skin.'),(14676,975,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Ice energy builds up in the horn on its upper jaw, causing the horn to reach cryogenic temperatures that freeze its surroundings.'),(14677,973,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon apparently ties the base of its neck into a knot so that energy stored in its belly does not escape from its beak.'),(14678,973,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Thanks to a behavior of theirs known as “synchronizing,” an entire flock of these Pokémon can attack simultaneously in perfect harmony.'),(14679,974,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This species left the ocean and began living on land a very long time ago. It seems to be closely related to Wailmer.'),(14680,974,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It lives in frigid regions in pods of five or so individuals. It loves the minerals found in snow and ice.'),(14681,982,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles.'),(14682,982,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It drives enemies out of its nest by sucking in enough air to fill its long, narrow lungs, then releasing the air in an intense blast.'),(14683,978,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This is a small dragon Pokémon. It lives inside the mouth of Dondozo to protect itself from enemies on the outside.'),(14684,978,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Tatsugiri is an extremely cunning Pokémon. It feigns weakness to lure in prey, then orders its partner to attack.'),(14685,976,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When Veluza discards unnecessary flesh, its mind becomes honed and its psychic power increases. The spare flesh has a mild but delicious flavor.'),(14686,976,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Veluza has excellent regenerative capabilities. It sheds spare flesh from its body to boost its agility, then charges at its prey.'),(14687,983,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Only a Bisharp that stands above all others in its vast army can evolve into Kingambit.'),(14688,983,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Though it commands a massive army in battle, it’s not skilled at devising complex strategies. It just uses brute strength to keep pushing.'),(14689,979,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When its anger rose beyond a critical point, this Pokémon gained power that is unfettered by the limits of its physical body.'),(14690,979,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It imbues its fists with the power of the rage that it kept hidden in its heart. Opponents struck by these imbued fists will be shattered to their core.'),(14691,977,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon is a glutton, but it’s bad at getting food. It teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.'),(14692,977,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It treats Tatsugiri like its boss and follows it loyally. Though powerful, Dondozo is apparently not very smart.'),(14693,981,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Now that the brain waves from the head and tail are synced up, the psychic power of this Pokémon is 10 times stronger than Girafarig’s.'),(14694,981,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The hardened head from the tail protects the head of the main body as Farigiraf whips its long neck around to headbutt enemies.'),(14695,980,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','When attacked, this Pokémon will retaliate by sticking thick spines out from its body. It’s a risky move that puts everything on the line.'),(14696,980,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It lives at the bottom of ponds and swamps. It will carry Wooper on its back and ferry them across water from one shore to the other.'),(14697,985,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','There has been only one reported sighting of this Pokémon. It resembles a mysterious creature depicted in an old expedition journal.'),(14698,985,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles a mysterious Pokémon described in a paranormal magazine as a Jigglypuff from one billion years ago.'),(14699,984,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. The name Great Tusk was taken from a creature listed in a certain book.'),(14700,984,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This creature resembles a mysterious Pokémon that, according to a paranormal magazine, has lived since ancient times.'),(14701,986,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It is possible that the creature listed as Brute Bonnet in a certain book could actually be this Pokémon.'),(14702,986,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It bears a slight resemblance to a Pokémon described in a dubious magazine as a cross between a dinosaur and a mushroom.'),(14703,987,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon has characteristics similar to those of Flutter Mane, a creature mentioned in a certain book.'),(14704,987,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has similar features to a ghostly pterosaur that was covered in a paranormal magazine, but the two have little else in common.'),(14705,989,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','No records exist of this Pokémon being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon’s traits match up with a creature shown in an expedition journal.'),(14706,989,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It slightly resembles a Magneton that lived for 10,000 years and was featured in an article in a paranormal magazine.'),(14707,988,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This mysterious Pokémon has some similarities to a creature that an old book introduced as Slither Wing.'),(14708,988,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon somewhat resembles an ancient form of Volcarona that was introduced in a dubious magazine.'),(14709,990,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon closely resembles a scientific weapon that a paranormal magazine claimed was sent to this planet by aliens.'),(14710,990,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. It resembles a mysterious object described in an old expedition journal.'),(14711,996,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Frigibax absorbs heat through its dorsal fin and converts the heat into ice energy. The higher the temperature, the more energy Frigibax stores.'),(14712,996,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon lives in forests and craggy areas. Using the power of its dorsal fin, it cools the inside of its nest like a refrigerator.'),(14713,994,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon resembles an unknown object described in a paranormal magazine as a UFO sent to observe humanity.'),(14714,994,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','No records exist of this species being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon’s traits match up with an object described in an old book.'),(14715,991,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its shape is similar to a robot featured in a paranormal magazine article. The robot was said to have been created by an ancient civilization.'),(14716,991,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles a mysterious object mentioned in an old book. There are only two reported sightings of this Pokémon.'),(14717,993,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles a certain Pokémon introduced in a paranormal magazine, described as the offspring of a Hydreigon that fell in love with a robot.'),(14718,993,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It’s possible that Iron Jugulis, an object described in an old book, may actually be this Pokémon.'),(14719,995,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has some similarities to a Pokémon introduced in a dubious magazine as a Tyranitar from one billion years into the future.'),(14720,995,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Some of its notable features match those of an object named within a certain expedition journal as Iron Thorns.'),(14721,992,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It is very similar to a cyborg covered exclusively by a paranormal magazine. The cyborg was said to be the modified form of a certain athlete.'),(14722,992,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon shares many similarities with Iron Hands, an object mentioned in a certain expedition journal.'),(14723,997,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Arctibax freezes the air around it, protecting its face with an ice mask and turning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice.'),(14724,997,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It attacks with the blade of its frozen dorsal fin by doing a front flip in the air. Arctibax’s strong back and legs allow it to pull off this technique.'),(14725,998,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air out from its mouth. This air can instantly freeze even liquid-hot lava.'),(14726,998,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It launches itself into battle by flipping upside down and spewing frigid air from its mouth. It finishes opponents off with its dorsal blade.'),(14727,1000,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its body seems to be made up of 1,000 coins. This Pokémon gets along well with others and is quick to make friends with anybody.'),(14728,1000,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has a sturdy body made up of stacked coins. Gholdengo overwhelms its enemies by firing coin after coin at them in quick succession.'),(14729,999,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon was born inside a treasure chest about 1,500 years ago. It sucks the life-force out of scoundrels who try to steal the treasure.'),(14730,999,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It lives inside an old treasure chest. Sometimes it gets left in shop corners since no one realizes it’s actually a Pokémon.'),(14731,1006,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It has some similarities to a mad scientist’s invention covered in a paranormal magazine.'),(14732,1006,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It’s possible that this is the object listed as Iron Valiant in a certain expedition journal.'),(14733,1003,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The fear poured into an ancient ritual vessel has clad itself in rocks and dirt to become a Pokémon.'),(14734,1003,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It slowly brings its exceedingly heavy head down upon the ground, splitting the earth open with huge fissures that run over 160 feet deep.'),(14735,1011,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Dipplin is two creatures in one Pokémon. Its evolution was triggered by a special apple grown only in one place.'),(14736,1011,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out.'),(14737,1002,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon can control 100 tons of fallen snow. It plays around innocently by leaping in and out of avalanches it has caused.'),(14738,1002,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The hatred of those who perished by the sword long ago has clad itself in snow and become a Pokémon.'),(14739,1001,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The grudge of a person punished for writing the king’s evil deeds upon wooden tablets has clad itself in dead leaves to become a Pokémon.'),(14740,1001,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It drains the life-force from vegetation, causing nearby forests to instantly wither and fields to turn barren.'),(14741,1005,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It is possible that this is the creature listed as Roaring Moon in an expedition journal that still holds many mysteries.'),(14742,1005,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','According to an article in a dubious magazine, this Pokémon has some connection to a phenomenon that occurs in a certain region.'),(14743,1007,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This seems to be the Winged King mentioned in an old expedition journal. It was said to have split the land with its bare fists.'),(14744,1007,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon resembles Cyclizar, but it is far burlier and more ferocious. Nothing is known about its ecology or other features.'),(14745,1004,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It controls flames burning at over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit. It casually swims through the sea of lava it creates by melting rock and sand.'),(14746,1004,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The envy accumulated within curved beads that sparked multiple conflicts has clad itself in fire and become a Pokémon.'),(14747,1008,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Much remains unknown about this creature. It resembles Cyclizar, but it is far more ruthless and powerful.'),(14748,1008,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This seems to be the Iron Serpent mentioned in an old book. The Iron Serpent is said to have turned the land to ash with its lightning.'),(14749,1010,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Many of its physical characteristics match those of a Virizion from the future that was covered in a paranormal magazine.'),(14750,1010,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','According to the few eyewitness accounts that exist, it used its shining blades to julienne large trees and boulders.'),(14751,1009,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This ferocious creature is shrouded in mystery. It\'s named after an aquatic monster mentioned in an old expedition journal.'),(14752,1009,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles an illustration published in a paranormal magazine, said to be a depiction of a super-ancient Suicune.'),(14753,1012,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Supposedly, the regrets of a tea ceremony master who died before perfecting his craft lingered in some matcha and became a Pokémon.'),(14754,1012,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Poltchageist looks like a regional form of Sinistea, but it was recently discovered that the two Pokémon are entirely unrelated.'),(14755,1015,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','The chain is made from toxins that enhance capabilities. It stimulated Munkidori\'s brain and caused the Pokémon\'s psychic powers to bloom.'),(14756,1015,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Munkidori keeps itself somewhere safe while it toys with its foes, using psychokinesis to induce intense dizziness.'),(14757,1013,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It pretends to be tea, trying to fool people into drinking it so it can drain their life-force. Its ruse is generally unsuccessful.'),(14758,1013,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It prefers cool, dark places, such as the back of a shelf or the space beneath a home\'s floorboards. It wanders in search of prey after sunset.'),(14759,1016,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Fezandipiti owes its beautiful looks and lovely voice to the toxic stimulants emanating from the chain wrapped around its body.'),(14760,1016,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Fezandipiti beats its glossy wings to scatter pheromones that captivate people and Pokémon.'),(14761,1019,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Seven syrpents live inside an apple made of syrup. The syrpent in the center is the commander.'),(14762,1019,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','These capricious syrpents have banded together. On the rare occasion that their moods align, their true power is unleashed.'),(14763,1018,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It gathers static electricity from its surroundings. The beams it launches when down on all fours are tremendously powerful.'),(14764,1018,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It digs holes on mountains, searching for food. It’s so durable that being caught in a cave-in won’t faze it.'),(14765,1014,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','After all its muscles were stimulated by the toxic chain around its neck, Okidogi transformed and gained a powerful physique.'),(14766,1014,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Okidogi is a ruffian with a short temper. It can pulverize anything by swinging around the chain on its neck.'),(14767,1017,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This Pokémon\'s type changes based on which mask it\'s wearing. It confounds its enemies with nimble movements and kicks.'),(14768,1017,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','This mischief-loving Pokémon is full of curiosity. It battles by drawing out the type-based energy contained within its masks.'),(14769,1020,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','There are scant few reports of this creature being sighted. One short video shows it rampaging and spouting pillars of flame.'),(14770,1020,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles an eerie Pokémon once shown in a paranormal magazine. That Pokémon was said to be an Entei regenerated from a fossil.'),(14771,1021,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It\'s said to incinerate everything around it with lightning launched from its fur. Very little is known about this creature.'),(14772,1021,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It bears resemblance to a Pokémon that became a hot topic for a short while after a paranormal magazine touted it as Raikou\'s ancestor.'),(14773,1023,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles a mysterious object introduced in a paranormal magazine as a cutting-edge weapon shaped like a Cobalion.'),(14774,1023,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','There was supposedly an incident in which it launched shining blades to cut everything around it to pieces. Little else is known about it.'),(14775,1025,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It feeds others toxic mochi that draw out desires and capabilities. Those who eat the mochi fall under Pecharunt’s control, chained to its will.'),(14776,1025,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Its peach-shaped shell serves as storage for a potent poison. It makes poisonous mochi and serves them to people and Pokémon.'),(14777,1024,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','Terapagos protects itself using its power to transform energy into hard crystals. This Pokémon is the source of the Terastal phenomenon.'),(14778,1024,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It’s thought that this Pokémon lived in ancient Paldea until it got caught in seismic shifts and went extinct.'),(14779,1022,'scarlet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It resembles a Pokémon described in a dubious magazine as a Terrakion that had been modified by an evil organization.'),(14780,1022,'violet','Gen IX (Paldea)','It was named after a mysterious object recorded in an old book. Its body seems to be metallic.');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `pokemon_lore` ENABLE KEYS */;
